1
00:04:30,188 --> 00:04:31,355
The truth is dead.

2
00:04:34,771 --> 00:04:35,938
The truth is dead.

3
00:04:37,271 --> 00:04:38,271
The truth has died

4
00:04:38,688 --> 00:04:41,521
and turned this house into a graveyard.

5
00:05:47,688 --> 00:05:50,313
The truth is dead.

6
00:06:08,688 --> 00:06:09,980
Good Morning, Ap…

7
00:06:14,105 --> 00:06:15,021
Appa.

8
00:06:19,396 --> 00:06:20,355
Appa?

9
00:06:21,563 --> 00:06:22,563
Appa?

10
00:06:25,105 --> 00:06:25,980
Appa?

11
00:06:26,105 --> 00:06:27,063
Appa?

12
00:06:28,396 --> 00:06:29,730
Lavana sir!

13
00:06:34,355 --> 00:06:35,230
Hello?

14
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,854
Doctor is on his morning rounds.

15
00:06:38,855 --> 00:06:39,771
He can't talk right now.

16
00:06:40,521 --> 00:06:42,730
Open your mouth once, please.

17
00:07:03,230 --> 00:07:04,105
Ma'am?

18
00:07:04,771 --> 00:07:06,646
- How are you feeling now?
- Better, sir.

19
00:07:07,021 --> 00:07:09,480
Good! You are doing very well.

20
00:07:09,771 --> 00:07:11,313
<i>You have nothing to worry about.</i>

21
00:07:11,563 --> 00:07:12,521
Just wait and watch.

22
00:07:12,896 --> 00:07:15,855
You'll be up and home in 2 days.

23
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:20,687
<i>She totally bought that lie, doctor.</i>

24
00:07:20,688 --> 00:07:22,937
<i>She thinks she'll live to 100 now.</i>

25
00:07:22,938 --> 00:07:24,605
A lie is like a sweet melody.

26
00:07:25,063 --> 00:07:26,980
It's music to the ears.

27
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:31,480
A sweet lie is better than
a troubling truth, junior.

28
00:07:32,313 --> 00:07:34,355
A doctor's job is to offer relief.

29
00:07:34,771 --> 00:07:36,021
Not to cause more pain.

30
00:07:36,646 --> 00:07:39,396
She has only four days left to live.

31
00:07:40,688 --> 00:07:43,730
Call her son in an hour
and ask him to take her home.

32
00:07:44,521 --> 00:07:45,521
Let us see this ward.

33
00:07:47,563 --> 00:07:48,438
Doctor!

34
00:07:53,188 --> 00:07:54,812
Doctor, there's a phone call for you.

35
00:07:54,813 --> 00:07:57,355
Not when I'm with the patients.

36
00:07:57,896 --> 00:07:58,813
Don't you know?

37
00:07:59,271 --> 00:08:00,521
Note their details.

38
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:01,896
Tell them I'll call back later.

39
00:08:02,105 --> 00:08:04,313
I did tell them, sir.
But they're saying it's urgent.

40
00:08:04,855 --> 00:08:06,105
Who's in such a hurry?

41
00:08:06,438 --> 00:08:07,563
It's Mr. Lavanappa Raju, sir.

42
00:08:08,813 --> 00:08:09,688
Lavana?

43
00:08:11,521 --> 00:08:13,605
You start examining this ward.
I'll join you.

44
00:08:15,313 --> 00:08:16,188
Junior!

45
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:20,438
Don't tell them the truth.
It'll scare them.

46
00:08:25,646 --> 00:08:26,980
{\an8}- Hello?
<i>- Uncle?</i>

47
00:08:27,313 --> 00:08:29,313
{\an8}- It's Lavana.
- Tell me, Lavana?

48
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:31,688
<i>You need to come to our house urgently.</i>

49
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,730
Dad wants to discuss
something personal with you.

50
00:08:35,105 --> 00:08:36,521
This early in the morning?

51
00:08:37,730 --> 00:08:38,937
Is your father fine, Lavana?

52
00:08:38,938 --> 00:08:41,604
He fell unconscious again this morning.

53
00:08:41,605 --> 00:08:43,521
{\an8}It's a miracle he's still alive, sir.

54
00:08:43,688 --> 00:08:45,063
Please don't say that, doctor.

55
00:08:45,313 --> 00:08:47,105
The truth is often harsh, doctor.

56
00:08:47,438 --> 00:08:50,438
<i>I told you a year ago that
he wouldn't live beyond four months.</i>

57
00:08:50,688 --> 00:08:53,520
When he's questioning
35 years of my experience,

58
00:08:53,521 --> 00:08:55,938
{\an8}<i>what can I do but stay silent?</i>

59
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,562
I haven't seen anyone live this long…

60
00:08:58,563 --> 00:09:00,313
with end-stage liver cancer.

61
00:09:00,563 --> 00:09:03,062
<i>And that too, while still drinking.</i>

62
00:09:03,063 --> 00:09:06,770
I'm insisting on a hospital visit
just to see this super-human.

63
00:09:06,771 --> 00:09:08,520
<i>There's nothing really that I can do.</i>

64
00:09:08,521 --> 00:09:10,437
Why don't you do one thing?

65
00:09:10,438 --> 00:09:11,520
Tell me, doctor.

66
00:09:11,521 --> 00:09:14,813
{\an8}Try sending him to a rehab
in America to quit alcohol.

67
00:09:15,563 --> 00:09:18,229
I don't know.
He is already a man of miracles.

68
00:09:18,230 --> 00:09:20,354
That will lead to more complications.

69
00:09:20,355 --> 00:09:22,062
<i>You see, Dr. Achari.</i>

70
00:09:22,063 --> 00:09:26,062
He's an alcoholic with
an undiagnosed psychological disorder.

71
00:09:26,063 --> 00:09:30,937
<i>He suffers from
phobias, delusions, and hallucinations.</i>

72
00:09:30,938 --> 00:09:34,229
He uses alcohol to numb these symptoms.

73
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:36,980
If you try to make him quit now,

74
00:09:37,271 --> 00:09:39,270
won't the withdrawal worsen his symptoms?

75
00:09:39,271 --> 00:09:40,355
What do you suggest then?

76
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:44,230
<i>First, we need to diagnose
his mental disorder.</i>

77
00:09:44,438 --> 00:09:47,771
{\an8}Second, is his disorder genetic…

78
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:52,479
{\an8}or was it caused by trauma?

79
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,854
{\an8}This is what we need to figure out.

80
00:09:53,855 --> 00:09:57,229
{\an8}Then he needs to be on medication
and go through therapy.

81
00:09:57,230 --> 00:09:59,562
{\an8}In order to do any of this,

82
00:09:59,563 --> 00:10:01,729
{\an8}you need to first bring him to me, doctor.

83
00:10:01,730 --> 00:10:08,730
BHUVANA'S ESTATE

84
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:49,313
So, Achchamma? How are you?

85
00:10:49,605 --> 00:10:51,855
Just getting by, sir.

86
00:10:52,813 --> 00:10:54,230
What do you mean "getting by"?

87
00:10:54,938 --> 00:10:55,938
Aren't you keeping well?

88
00:10:56,730 --> 00:10:58,771
Sir's condition has
gotten me worried, sir.

89
00:10:59,271 --> 00:11:00,813
Of course, I'm not fine.

90
00:11:04,021 --> 00:11:04,896
Greetings, sir.

91
00:11:06,230 --> 00:11:08,145
Who's that?
I've never seen her here before.

92
00:11:08,146 --> 00:11:09,605
She's my daughter-in-law, sir.

93
00:11:09,938 --> 00:11:12,438
All the servants quit, one by one.

94
00:11:13,855 --> 00:11:17,646
So, I brought her in for help.

95
00:11:19,938 --> 00:11:22,896
Coming back to the point,
what happened to your Appa?

96
00:11:23,521 --> 00:11:24,813
You know how it is, sir.

97
00:11:25,105 --> 00:11:26,605
It's the same story every night.

98
00:11:27,271 --> 00:11:30,563
The memories of his younger
son are eating him up inside.

99
00:11:31,063 --> 00:11:31,938
That's not all.

100
00:11:32,396 --> 00:11:34,521
He keeps screaming "Kusuma! Kusuma!"

101
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:36,688
loudly in his sleep.

102
00:11:43,521 --> 00:11:45,105
Has she been out lately?

103
00:11:53,230 --> 00:11:54,105
Go on.

104
00:11:55,896 --> 00:11:58,855
I guess he missed his
son more than usual today.

105
00:11:59,688 --> 00:12:01,980
He cried and cried
until he fell unconscious.

106
00:12:13,396 --> 00:12:16,270
Do you know all this for sure,
or do you just think you do?

107
00:12:16,271 --> 00:12:18,645
Oh, please, sir.
You never believe me.

108
00:12:18,646 --> 00:12:20,021
Why would I make something like that up?

109
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:25,605
Only you would know that!

110
00:12:28,730 --> 00:12:30,771
- Is he in the room?
- Yeah, he is. Go!

111
00:12:31,688 --> 00:12:33,270
Where else would he be?

112
00:12:33,271 --> 00:12:34,813
"Is he in the room?" he asks.

113
00:12:35,021 --> 00:12:37,313
He's been this way since childhood.
He has never trusted me.

114
00:12:48,605 --> 00:12:50,230
Injustice has prevailed.

115
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:54,063
The 'Kauravas' have been betrayed.

116
00:12:56,563 --> 00:12:57,980
How can the 'Pandavas' take the throne?

117
00:12:59,271 --> 00:13:00,146
They can't.

118
00:13:01,355 --> 00:13:02,271
They shouldn't.

119
00:13:04,146 --> 00:13:06,188
The heirs of a 'nobody'
have ruled the kingdom.

120
00:13:09,646 --> 00:13:11,146
He wasn't fortunate
enough to have children.

121
00:13:11,771 --> 00:13:13,105
He would die if he tried.

122
00:13:14,646 --> 00:13:16,438
No! No! No! No! No!

123
00:13:17,313 --> 00:13:18,396
A mistake has been made.

124
00:13:19,271 --> 00:13:20,480
A mistake has been made.

125
00:13:26,521 --> 00:13:27,480
You, lady!

126
00:13:28,313 --> 00:13:29,855
Were the Pandavas born to him?

127
00:13:31,521 --> 00:13:32,521
Or you tell me, lady!

128
00:13:33,105 --> 00:13:34,813
Were they his biological sons?

129
00:13:35,646 --> 00:13:37,021
Why don't you answer me?

130
00:13:37,813 --> 00:13:39,480
Were Pandavas really born to him?!

131
00:13:40,063 --> 00:13:42,480
Why won't you believe when I say so?

132
00:13:42,771 --> 00:13:44,605
The Pandavas were not born to him.

133
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:48,187
- They weren't born to him.
- Hey, Ramudu!

134
00:13:48,188 --> 00:13:51,521
- They weren't! They weren't!
- Ramudu! Don't hit yourself!

135
00:13:51,938 --> 00:13:52,896
Ramudu!

136
00:13:58,730 --> 00:14:00,605
Were the Pandavas born to him?

137
00:14:02,896 --> 00:14:03,813
No, they weren't.

138
00:14:04,438 --> 00:14:06,021
Then why won't they answer me?

139
00:14:10,355 --> 00:14:11,313
Who?

140
00:14:12,855 --> 00:14:13,813
They're not here anymore.

141
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:16,688
They left because they
don't have an answer for me.

142
00:14:17,771 --> 00:14:20,146
Who is it this time?

143
00:14:21,438 --> 00:14:24,188
It was them. Kunti and Madri.

144
00:14:25,271 --> 00:14:26,605
- And…
- Kunti?

145
00:14:27,605 --> 00:14:28,688
How did you even enter…

146
00:14:29,730 --> 00:14:31,063
when the walls are rotating?

147
00:14:32,605 --> 00:14:34,271
It's not the walls that are rotating.

148
00:14:36,438 --> 00:14:38,480
I came in with them.

149
00:14:40,771 --> 00:14:41,855
I didn't notice you.

150
00:14:42,063 --> 00:14:42,938
It's fine.

151
00:14:43,313 --> 00:14:44,896
You seemed busy with them.

152
00:14:47,771 --> 00:14:48,688
With whom?

153
00:14:50,105 --> 00:14:53,355
With Kunti and Madri.

154
00:14:53,563 --> 00:14:54,521
Is it?

155
00:14:55,646 --> 00:14:57,187
Were they here? Are they here?

156
00:14:57,188 --> 00:14:58,730
Where are they?

157
00:14:59,271 --> 00:15:02,396
- Where are they?
- They feared you and ran away.

158
00:15:04,855 --> 00:15:05,895
Tell me if they come again.

159
00:15:05,896 --> 00:15:07,229
I need to ask some questions.

160
00:15:07,230 --> 00:15:08,146
Alright.

161
00:15:08,438 --> 00:15:10,730
I'll tell you. Sit down calmly first.

162
00:15:11,396 --> 00:15:12,271
Sit.

163
00:15:15,313 --> 00:15:18,396
What's with these creepers and pumpkins?

164
00:15:18,771 --> 00:15:20,438
Didn't I ask you to get these removed?

165
00:15:20,855 --> 00:15:21,730
Don't touch them!

166
00:15:22,271 --> 00:15:23,230
Let them be.

167
00:15:24,396 --> 00:15:26,396
I hoped my second son
would look like a pumpkin too.

168
00:15:27,105 --> 00:15:28,605
Let them grow, at least.

169
00:15:34,438 --> 00:15:36,146
Why did you ask for me?

170
00:15:36,896 --> 00:15:37,813
Me?

171
00:15:40,021 --> 00:15:41,146
I didn't ask you to come.

172
00:15:41,855 --> 00:15:42,813
You didn't?

173
00:15:43,605 --> 00:15:46,730
But Lavana said you wanted
to talk to me personally.

174
00:15:47,188 --> 00:15:48,896
That guy? He always does this.

175
00:15:49,021 --> 00:15:51,562
He blames me for things I don't do.

176
00:15:51,563 --> 00:15:53,438
- He hates me for some reason.
- Yeah, fine.

177
00:15:56,855 --> 00:15:58,770
I came here to talk to you.

178
00:15:58,771 --> 00:16:00,646
Then, why are you silent?
Spill it!

179
00:16:01,313 --> 00:16:04,438
I want you to come and
see the doctor with me.

180
00:16:09,396 --> 00:16:10,855
You are my doctor, right?

181
00:16:11,521 --> 00:16:12,771
Why go to someone else?

182
00:16:13,396 --> 00:16:16,187
- I'm just a general doctor. You…
- Yes, I know, I know.

183
00:16:16,188 --> 00:16:19,188
You'll take me to a cancer doctor
or a mental doctor, right?

184
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:22,145
Not a mental doctor.
A psychiatrist.

185
00:16:22,146 --> 00:16:23,895
Yeah! Psychiatrist!
Psychiatrist! Psychiatrist!

186
00:16:23,896 --> 00:16:25,229
Some big psychiatrist!

187
00:16:25,230 --> 00:16:27,937
I won't come. I won't come.
He doesn't know anything.

188
00:16:27,938 --> 00:16:28,980
Am I crazy to go there?

189
00:16:29,521 --> 00:16:30,480
I look sane, right?

190
00:16:32,188 --> 00:16:33,520
I'm not coming. No way!

191
00:16:33,521 --> 00:16:34,605
Fine. Don't come!

192
00:16:36,146 --> 00:16:37,063
Don't come.

193
00:16:44,063 --> 00:16:45,687
Consult the cancer doctor at least?

194
00:16:45,688 --> 00:16:46,937
No, I won't come. I won't come.

195
00:16:46,938 --> 00:16:48,730
He doesn't know anything.
It's a waste of money.

196
00:16:49,105 --> 00:16:51,229
A year ago, he told me
I'd die in four months.

197
00:16:51,230 --> 00:16:52,896
I didn't die, did I?

198
00:16:54,646 --> 00:16:56,479
I won't come! I won't come! I won't come!

199
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,813
He doesn't know anything. He doesn't.

200
00:16:58,021 --> 00:17:00,188
- He doesn't know anything.
- Yes, he doesn't know anything.

201
00:17:00,730 --> 00:17:02,312
- Don't get any closer.
- He doesn't know anything.

202
00:17:02,313 --> 00:17:03,979
That's why he's puzzled
you're still alive!

203
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:06,313
He longs for your holy presence.

204
00:17:08,563 --> 00:17:11,104
You won't die, will you?

205
00:17:11,105 --> 00:17:12,480
But you'll drive us to death instead.

206
00:17:13,438 --> 00:17:14,646
One day at a time.

207
00:17:36,105 --> 00:17:37,688
Sorry, Achari.

208
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,938
I shouldn't have called you and
hurt you like this.

209
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:44,855
So, you asked me to come?

210
00:17:45,188 --> 00:17:47,312
Yes, didn't Lavana tell you?

211
00:17:47,313 --> 00:17:48,605
He always does this.

212
00:17:48,896 --> 00:17:51,354
I pampered him so much
for being my only son,

213
00:17:51,355 --> 00:17:54,105
- and he turned out so useless.
- Don't go down that road.

214
00:17:55,271 --> 00:17:58,563
Leave it. Tell me why you called
before you forget.

215
00:18:00,438 --> 00:18:02,105
Sit. I'll tell you.

216
00:18:02,730 --> 00:18:03,896
I'm sitting. Tell me.

217
00:18:05,521 --> 00:18:08,563
You're all wondering how
I'm still alive, right?

218
00:18:11,188 --> 00:18:12,105
Yes.

219
00:18:13,313 --> 00:18:14,396
I know why.

220
00:18:15,730 --> 00:18:16,688
What do you know?

221
00:18:18,646 --> 00:18:19,563
I have…

222
00:18:21,063 --> 00:18:23,729
I've been possessed by a demon, Achari.

223
00:18:23,730 --> 00:18:28,229
- Hey! You're speaking nonsense again.
- No, it makes sense.

224
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:30,688
I'll explain it to you. Sit down once.

225
00:18:32,021 --> 00:18:32,896
Tell me.

226
00:18:34,313 --> 00:18:38,438
Remember "Fill in the Blanks" from school?

227
00:18:40,021 --> 00:18:41,021
I remember.

228
00:18:42,105 --> 00:18:45,188
"Dash" is a deadly demon.
Fill in the blank.

229
00:18:47,896 --> 00:18:50,438
Doubt is a deadly demon.

230
00:18:52,271 --> 00:18:55,271
That's the demon I'm possessed with.

231
00:18:55,563 --> 00:18:56,980
Doubt is a drug.

232
00:18:57,188 --> 00:18:59,063
I won't die till its high wears off.

233
00:18:59,438 --> 00:19:01,855
What are you doubtful about?

234
00:19:05,188 --> 00:19:06,605
He's listening.

235
00:19:10,313 --> 00:19:11,230
Hey!

236
00:19:11,771 --> 00:19:12,771
You little rascal!

237
00:19:13,521 --> 00:19:14,730
I know it's you!

238
00:19:16,271 --> 00:19:17,980
How dare you spy on me
in my own house?

239
00:19:18,521 --> 00:19:19,396
Hey!

240
00:19:20,313 --> 00:19:21,188
Where are you?

241
00:19:23,938 --> 00:19:26,855
Wait, I'll have Achari deal with you.

242
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,438
<i>Who's that?</i>

243
00:19:28,855 --> 00:19:31,730
It's Kusuma, man.

244
00:19:33,688 --> 00:19:35,521
- Kusuma?
- Yes.

245
00:19:36,271 --> 00:19:38,312
Even though my body has given up,

246
00:19:38,313 --> 00:19:42,730
it's doubt that's kept
my soul trapped in a jar.

247
00:19:43,105 --> 00:19:44,896
Please fulfill my last wish and

248
00:19:45,188 --> 00:19:48,938
free me from the curse of this jar.

249
00:19:59,521 --> 00:20:00,771
Did you read this?

250
00:20:01,021 --> 00:20:03,480
They're running blood tests to
identify the biological parents.

251
00:20:04,813 --> 00:20:05,979
{\an8}You are a doctor, right?

252
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:08,563
Take my blood and find out
if Kusuma is my son.

253
00:20:08,730 --> 00:20:09,605
Here.

254
00:20:10,813 --> 00:20:12,230
Take it. Take my blood.

255
00:20:13,313 --> 00:20:14,855
Hey! Ramudu!

256
00:20:15,355 --> 00:20:16,271
Ramudu, stop it!

257
00:20:16,563 --> 00:20:19,355
Your blood alone won't do.
We need his too.

258
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:21,813
How will you get a dead boy's blood?
Ramudu!

259
00:20:29,021 --> 00:20:30,146
What have you turned into, man?

260
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,188
See, you're bleeding!

261
00:20:45,896 --> 00:20:47,521
Why did this doubt even arise?

262
00:20:48,730 --> 00:20:50,521
So, the test is not possible?

263
00:20:50,938 --> 00:20:53,605
Look, Kusuma died eight years ago.

264
00:20:54,021 --> 00:20:55,688
How can we get his blood now?

265
00:20:56,688 --> 00:20:59,105
You promised to fulfill my last wish.

266
00:20:59,396 --> 00:21:01,813
- Yes, but
- Is there no other way?

267
00:21:03,146 --> 00:21:07,105
I'm not sure.
See, DNA testing is a new science.

268
00:21:07,355 --> 00:21:09,313
The world is just discovering it.

269
00:21:10,355 --> 00:21:12,813
Is there no way to test
without his blood?

270
00:21:13,688 --> 00:21:15,188
That's what I've been saying.
I don't know.

271
00:21:15,771 --> 00:21:18,105
But as a doctor who's
studied the human body,

272
00:21:18,230 --> 00:21:20,729
they'd need some sample
from the body, if not blood.

273
00:21:20,730 --> 00:21:22,063
But I can't guarantee anything.

274
00:21:22,438 --> 00:21:24,730
So, stop this nonsense
and come see the doctor.

275
00:21:25,813 --> 00:21:27,604
A psychiatrist can help
eliminate those thoughts.

276
00:21:27,605 --> 00:21:28,563
You may leave now.

277
00:22:03,813 --> 00:22:04,688
How are you?

278
00:22:10,313 --> 00:22:12,813
He's hanging between life and death.

279
00:22:15,396 --> 00:22:18,355
If you stop being stubborn
and talk to him,

280
00:22:18,855 --> 00:22:19,896
it may do him good.

281
00:22:28,938 --> 00:22:29,896
What is it, uncle?

282
00:22:30,355 --> 00:22:32,563
Did my dad scare you?

283
00:22:32,896 --> 00:22:34,813
You seem to have zoned out.

284
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:37,021
Eat, eat.

285
00:22:42,146 --> 00:22:43,521
What else is happening, Lavana?

286
00:22:43,730 --> 00:22:45,438
I'm applying for an American visa.

287
00:22:45,730 --> 00:22:47,646
- I'll leave once it gets approved.
- Oh.

288
00:22:49,188 --> 00:22:50,563
I remember you telling me.

289
00:22:53,021 --> 00:22:54,688
With all the property you'll inherit,

290
00:22:55,188 --> 00:22:57,896
why would you work
under someone in America?

291
00:22:58,688 --> 00:23:01,605
What's the point of all this inheritance?

292
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:03,396
She won't talk to me.

293
00:23:03,521 --> 00:23:05,396
I don't understand a thing he says.

294
00:23:05,646 --> 00:23:08,730
Instead of enduring his daily antics,

295
00:23:09,063 --> 00:23:10,813
I'd rather leave.

296
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:14,146
What if something happens
to him after you leave?

297
00:23:14,271 --> 00:23:17,146
They gave him a year, and so I waited.

298
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,938
Sinners don't die that easily, uncle.

299
00:23:19,188 --> 00:23:21,063
He put my mom through hell.

300
00:23:21,688 --> 00:23:23,105
He doesn't seem to be dying anytime soon.

301
00:23:24,105 --> 00:23:26,105
I've known you since
you were a kid, Lavana.

302
00:23:27,396 --> 00:23:29,605
Will you be hateful of everyone forever?

303
00:23:34,938 --> 00:23:38,688
Growing up, people teased
me for being premature.

304
00:23:39,230 --> 00:23:41,063
Premature babies come with flaws, right?

305
00:23:42,896 --> 00:23:44,063
‘Hateful', he says.

306
00:23:44,438 --> 00:23:46,855
Love doesn't always have
to be on display, like yours is.

307
00:23:47,146 --> 00:23:49,521
There is love in my concern for him.

308
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:51,104
I love him enough…

309
00:23:51,105 --> 00:23:53,188
to tolerate his torture
while giving medicines.

310
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,480
But lately,

311
00:23:56,271 --> 00:23:58,146
as I watch him struggling to stay alive,

312
00:23:58,271 --> 00:24:01,605
my love makes me want
to put him out of his misery.

313
00:24:03,271 --> 00:24:04,563
I'm running away before I do that.

314
00:24:05,605 --> 00:24:06,979
‘Hateful', he says.

315
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:09,229
As someone who visits once in a while,

316
00:24:09,230 --> 00:24:10,730
how would you know the pain we go through?

317
00:24:13,855 --> 00:24:17,021
He's confined himself in
his room like a madman.

318
00:24:17,146 --> 00:24:19,979
If I keep worrying about him,
I'll end up the same way.

319
00:24:19,980 --> 00:24:21,271
That's why I'm leaving.

320
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:25,396
Did he just call me mad?

321
00:24:25,855 --> 00:24:26,855
Who's mad?

322
00:24:28,563 --> 00:24:29,605
He thinks I'm mad?

323
00:24:30,105 --> 00:24:32,146
Saying I confined myself to the room.

324
00:24:40,730 --> 00:24:43,813
The world seems so vast when we're young.

325
00:24:44,230 --> 00:24:46,230
It shrinks as we grow.

326
00:24:46,896 --> 00:24:48,563
We think it's because
we've grown physically.

327
00:24:49,021 --> 00:24:51,355
But the truth is, we've
stopped growing mentally.

328
00:24:52,563 --> 00:24:54,563
I shut myself in my room, eh?

329
00:24:55,146 --> 00:24:56,146
What does he know about it?

330
00:24:57,855 --> 00:25:00,480
Once upon a time, my world was vast too.

331
00:25:01,521 --> 00:25:04,604
If you turned my life into a film,
it would be two parts.

332
00:25:04,605 --> 00:25:05,896
At least two parts!

333
00:25:22,271 --> 00:25:23,937
I was a free bird out there.

334
00:25:23,938 --> 00:25:25,230
Why did you put me in this cage?

335
00:25:25,855 --> 00:25:29,813
<i>Your eyes might've witnessed</i>

336
00:25:30,646 --> 00:25:34,771
<i>many many ups and downs.</i>

337
00:25:35,355 --> 00:25:39,937
<i>This night, o wanderer,</i>

338
00:25:39,938 --> 00:25:44,895
<i>come, see this path.</i>

339
00:25:44,896 --> 00:25:47,312
<i>Any man's life is ruined,</i>

340
00:25:47,313 --> 00:25:49,729
<i>if he doesn't travel</i>

341
00:25:49,730 --> 00:25:51,813
<i>He knowingly</i>

342
00:25:52,063 --> 00:25:53,979
<i>falls in the traps.</i>

343
00:25:53,980 --> 00:25:56,604
<i>The world around
us, filled with norms,</i>

344
00:25:56,605 --> 00:25:58,645
<i>will the hungry soul
stop, even if you try?</i>

345
00:25:58,646 --> 00:26:01,270
<i>If you sprinkle water
in the name of morals,</i>

346
00:26:01,271 --> 00:26:03,604
<i>will this raging thirst calm down?</i>

347
00:26:03,605 --> 00:26:07,313
<i>I will engulf you in waves of beauty.</i>

348
00:26:08,271 --> 00:26:13,187
<i>I will trap you in my embrace.</i>

349
00:26:13,188 --> 00:26:14,979
<i>O explorer of the lands,</i>

350
00:26:14,980 --> 00:26:18,438
<i>will you explore my body?</i>

351
00:26:22,438 --> 00:26:24,687
<i>O universal beauty,</i>

352
00:26:24,688 --> 00:26:27,645
<i>I will dance with you in joy</i>

353
00:26:27,646 --> 00:26:29,313
<i>Rock and roll!</i>

354
00:26:29,646 --> 00:26:31,813
<i>Rock and roll!</i>

355
00:26:32,396 --> 00:26:34,812
<i>Rock and roll!
Rock and roll!</i>

356
00:26:34,813 --> 00:26:36,688
<i>Rock and rock and roll!</i>

357
00:27:10,605 --> 00:27:12,562
<i>Crossing mountains,
valleys and rivers,</i>

358
00:27:12,563 --> 00:27:15,104
{\an8}<i>climbing many peaks,</i>

359
00:27:15,105 --> 00:27:18,271
{\an8}<i>didn't it make you even a bit tired?</i>

360
00:27:19,771 --> 00:27:22,395
<i>A horse that wanders in the forest,</i>

361
00:27:22,396 --> 00:27:24,937
<i>a life with hope and spirit,</i>

362
00:27:24,938 --> 00:27:28,146
<i>should it not tread carefully?</i>

363
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:32,104
<i>If there's no freedom on this land,</i>

364
00:27:32,105 --> 00:27:34,520
<i>does it matter how long we live?</i>

365
00:27:34,521 --> 00:27:36,937
<i>What's the point of stopping</i>

366
00:27:36,938 --> 00:27:39,021
<i>after I learn this truth?</i>

367
00:27:39,188 --> 00:27:41,770
<i>Even a horse that gallops excitedly</i>

368
00:27:41,771 --> 00:27:44,020
<i>has to halt at a beautiful garden,</i>

369
00:27:44,021 --> 00:27:45,855
<i>to drive away his exhaustion and</i>

370
00:27:46,063 --> 00:27:48,354
<i>fulfill his needs.</i>

371
00:27:48,355 --> 00:27:51,187
<i>The world around
us, filled with norms,</i>

372
00:27:51,188 --> 00:27:53,270
<i>will the hungry soul
stop, even if you try?</i>

373
00:27:53,271 --> 00:27:55,895
<i>Even if you hold it in a cage,</i>

374
00:27:55,896 --> 00:27:58,020
<i>will this raging thirst calm down?</i>

375
00:27:58,021 --> 00:28:01,980
<i>I will engulf you in waves of my beauty</i>

376
00:28:02,855 --> 00:28:07,979
<i>I will trap you in my embrace.</i>

377
00:28:07,980 --> 00:28:09,563
<i>O explorer of the lands,</i>

378
00:28:09,688 --> 00:28:13,105
<i>will you explore my body?</i>

379
00:28:17,105 --> 00:28:19,312
<i>O universal beauty,</i>

380
00:28:19,313 --> 00:28:22,271
<i>I will dance with you in joy</i>

381
00:28:31,521 --> 00:28:33,687
<i>O universal beauty,</i>

382
00:28:33,688 --> 00:28:36,562
<i>I will dance with you in joy</i>

383
00:28:36,563 --> 00:28:38,645
<i>- Rock and roll!
- Rock and roll!</i>

384
00:28:38,646 --> 00:28:43,729
<i>Hey, rock and roll!</i>

385
00:28:43,730 --> 00:28:46,105
<i>Rock and rock and roll!</i>

386
00:28:49,396 --> 00:28:51,105
<i>Mogambo Khush Hua!</i>

387
00:28:54,271 --> 00:28:55,563
This is the first chapter of my story.

388
00:28:55,813 --> 00:28:59,188
In this, I'm a tireless traveler,
like an early human.

389
00:29:00,688 --> 00:29:01,812
For five years,

390
00:29:01,813 --> 00:29:04,687
I was an aimless bird with
no attachments whatsoever.

391
00:29:04,688 --> 00:29:05,730
But my first mistake was…

392
00:29:08,271 --> 00:29:09,271
a discussion with this guy.

393
00:29:11,021 --> 00:29:12,563
How did you know I was here?

394
00:29:14,771 --> 00:29:16,021
It took me two months, man.

395
00:29:17,146 --> 00:29:20,605
London to Singapore, then to
Morocco, Switzerland, and France.

396
00:29:21,105 --> 00:29:25,646
My search led me to Brahmanda
Nagaram, and here I am!

397
00:29:25,813 --> 00:29:27,855
Wow, that's one long journey!

398
00:29:28,313 --> 00:29:29,938
You should have visited
Kasi and returned home.

399
00:29:30,355 --> 00:29:31,355
Why did you come here?

400
00:29:31,605 --> 00:29:32,480
Hey.

401
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:36,021
You're meeting a friend after ages.
Is this how you talk to him?

402
00:29:36,980 --> 00:29:37,855
Oh no!

403
00:29:38,396 --> 00:29:39,480
Forgive me, dear friend!

404
00:29:39,896 --> 00:29:42,188
May I know the true purpose of your visit?

405
00:29:42,646 --> 00:29:46,938
Your father has ordered to
see you at his palace, at once.

406
00:29:47,896 --> 00:29:49,521
I'm no cattle to be dragged back home.

407
00:29:50,271 --> 00:29:51,271
I don't want to return home.

408
00:29:51,688 --> 00:29:53,312
Why do you dislike us so much?

409
00:29:53,313 --> 00:29:54,230
I like you people.

410
00:29:54,521 --> 00:29:57,480
It's your meaningless
traditions that I dislike.

411
00:29:57,688 --> 00:30:00,605
Yeah, like your deeds
are rather meaningful.

412
00:30:01,271 --> 00:30:03,438
Got a glimpse of it last night.

413
00:30:04,063 --> 00:30:06,438
Yeah! What's wrong with that?

414
00:30:06,688 --> 00:30:09,563
A man and a woman dancing in joy.

415
00:30:11,438 --> 00:30:12,938
You haven't changed a bit, Ramappa.

416
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:17,230
Everyone is awaiting your return.

417
00:30:18,188 --> 00:30:19,146
Why don't you visit once?

418
00:30:19,438 --> 00:30:22,605
Your little tricks to make me
return home haven't changed either.

419
00:30:23,188 --> 00:30:25,605
I told you the world is
my home when I left.

420
00:30:26,146 --> 00:30:27,146
I'm not coming back.

421
00:30:27,646 --> 00:30:30,813
Hence, please save your precious time…

422
00:30:31,021 --> 00:30:32,688
and return to the fort immediately.

423
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:37,563
Can I ask you something?

424
00:30:40,021 --> 00:30:40,980
What?

425
00:30:42,646 --> 00:30:43,980
Do you remember your dad's face?

426
00:30:47,105 --> 00:30:49,563
Ramudu? Ramudu?

427
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:51,438
Ramudu!

428
00:30:54,438 --> 00:30:55,480
Appa?

429
00:31:04,563 --> 00:31:05,438
Come in.

430
00:31:08,313 --> 00:31:10,646
Ew! Why is the room so dirty--

431
00:31:23,355 --> 00:31:24,480
That's just how the room is.

432
00:31:25,105 --> 00:31:26,605
Appa is a bit crazy.

433
00:31:26,980 --> 00:31:28,896
He tends to scatter things everywhere.

434
00:31:29,230 --> 00:31:30,813
He won't let us clean it if he comes out.

435
00:31:30,938 --> 00:31:33,396
Let's clean before that. Come.

436
00:31:45,438 --> 00:31:47,521
Wow! A pumpkin!

437
00:31:48,521 --> 00:31:50,313
- Can I take this?
- He'll kill you.

438
00:31:51,938 --> 00:31:53,313
Don't touch a thing, and get over here.

439
00:32:05,313 --> 00:32:06,188
Mother-in-law?

440
00:32:06,896 --> 00:32:08,521
How did he go crazy?

441
00:32:12,396 --> 00:32:13,938
He's got ears like a bat.

442
00:32:14,230 --> 00:32:16,605
He can hear your thoughts too.

443
00:32:16,938 --> 00:32:19,355
I'll tell you later. Get to work.

444
00:32:27,271 --> 00:32:28,146
Appa?!

445
00:32:28,896 --> 00:32:29,771
Appa!

446
00:32:30,521 --> 00:32:31,480
<i>Appa!</i>

447
00:32:36,855 --> 00:32:40,605
The key you asked for is on this table.

448
00:32:42,813 --> 00:32:44,896
Appa had another son.

449
00:32:45,355 --> 00:32:46,980
His name was Kusumappa Raju.

450
00:32:47,271 --> 00:32:49,188
<i>He meant the world to Appa.</i>

451
00:32:49,813 --> 00:32:52,730
<i>The son brought good fortune with him.</i>

452
00:32:52,980 --> 00:32:56,980
<i>But Kusuma used to behave crazy.</i>

453
00:32:57,146 --> 00:32:58,355
<i>Does he not live here anymore?</i>

454
00:32:58,688 --> 00:32:59,855
Let me finish.

455
00:33:00,146 --> 00:33:02,230
I don't know what happened that day.

456
00:33:02,396 --> 00:33:09,063
he drowned in our estate pond and died.

457
00:33:09,646 --> 00:33:11,313
- Oh, my!
- Yes.

458
00:33:12,521 --> 00:33:15,395
Having lost his beloved son,

459
00:33:15,396 --> 00:33:17,396
Appa lost his mind.

460
00:33:17,521 --> 00:33:20,396
Renuka ma'am stopped
coming out of her room.

461
00:33:20,688 --> 00:33:23,145
- Did you see I left a key on that table?
- Yes.

462
00:33:23,146 --> 00:33:24,813
It's the key to Kusuma's room.

463
00:33:25,021 --> 00:33:27,813
I wonder why he asked
for it after all these years.

464
00:35:04,521 --> 00:35:05,396
Ma'am.

465
00:35:06,063 --> 00:35:09,646
I don't know why, but Appa
asked for Kusuma's room key.

466
00:35:10,271 --> 00:35:13,355
I gave it to him,
afraid he'd make a scene.

467
00:35:14,271 --> 00:35:17,563
I'm informing you just to be safe.

468
00:35:19,271 --> 00:35:20,188
She just won't listen!

469
00:35:33,813 --> 00:35:36,938
Hey! Who is it?! Huh?!

470
00:35:37,438 --> 00:35:38,355
Who is it?

471
00:35:41,938 --> 00:35:43,313
Hey, Kusuma.

472
00:35:44,771 --> 00:35:47,396
You figured I'm in your room, didn't you?

473
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:52,021
Spying on me in my own house, eh?

474
00:36:56,813 --> 00:37:00,688
BHUVANA'S ESTATE

475
00:37:15,313 --> 00:37:16,188
Jangayya?

476
00:37:17,105 --> 00:37:17,980
Who is that woman?

477
00:37:18,355 --> 00:37:19,813
I don't know, Appa. Never seen her before.

478
00:37:24,605 --> 00:37:25,480
Excuse me?

479
00:37:26,188 --> 00:37:27,063
May I know who you are?

480
00:37:27,313 --> 00:37:29,562
I'm Mr. Siddappa's new nurse.

481
00:37:29,563 --> 00:37:30,730
Dr. Achari sent me.

482
00:37:36,438 --> 00:37:39,396
Achari sir didn't want to give
you bad news right off the bat.

483
00:37:39,563 --> 00:37:42,980
So he told me not to say
anything till you got home.

484
00:37:43,396 --> 00:37:45,646
Siddappa sir is bedridden and in a coma.

485
00:37:45,938 --> 00:37:49,396
Achari sir whispered in his ears that…

486
00:37:49,563 --> 00:37:51,688
you're married, and you're
visiting with your wife soon.

487
00:37:51,896 --> 00:37:53,521
But you showed up alone.

488
00:37:56,646 --> 00:37:57,521
Hello?

489
00:37:58,396 --> 00:38:00,063
There is a long way to go. Get in.

490
00:38:03,855 --> 00:38:04,730
Hey, you.

491
00:38:05,521 --> 00:38:06,937
I was minding my way.

492
00:38:06,938 --> 00:38:08,980
You stopped me to ask who I
was, and I answered out of courtesy.

493
00:38:09,271 --> 00:38:11,730
Shouldn't you tell me who you
are before asking me to hop in?

494
00:38:25,396 --> 00:38:26,480
I'm Mr. Siddappa's son.

495
00:38:26,980 --> 00:38:28,563
Oho! Nice to meet you.

496
00:38:30,730 --> 00:38:32,645
Glad to meet you too. And your name?

497
00:38:32,646 --> 00:38:33,521
I'm--

498
00:38:36,896 --> 00:38:37,980
Why did you stop?

499
00:38:39,688 --> 00:38:41,605
Oh, oh, okay.

500
00:38:42,605 --> 00:38:44,188
I'm sorry. I get it.

501
00:38:45,521 --> 00:38:46,855
My name is Ramappa.

502
00:38:48,355 --> 00:38:49,271
And you are?

503
00:38:49,396 --> 00:38:51,770
Now, that's courteous. I'm Renuka.

504
00:38:51,771 --> 00:38:52,688
Renuka.

505
00:38:54,605 --> 00:38:56,521
Now that formalities are out of the way,

506
00:38:57,188 --> 00:38:58,230
will you get in the car now?

507
00:38:59,938 --> 00:39:00,855
Now, I don't mind.

508
00:39:26,646 --> 00:39:27,605
Dad!

509
00:39:29,313 --> 00:39:30,271
What is it, Ramappa?

510
00:39:31,980 --> 00:39:33,230
Happy birthday, Dad.

511
00:39:33,771 --> 00:39:34,979
Thank you, Ramappa.

512
00:39:34,980 --> 00:39:36,313
Here is your birthday gift.

513
00:39:37,188 --> 00:39:40,063
- What is this?
- It's a poem I wrote for you.

514
00:39:42,605 --> 00:39:44,605
Go on. Read it for me.

515
00:39:45,980 --> 00:39:47,020
<i>O father!</i>

516
00:39:47,021 --> 00:39:49,438
<i>I do not fear the dark,</i>

517
00:39:50,063 --> 00:39:52,521
<i>so long as your smile stays by me.</i>

518
00:39:53,855 --> 00:39:56,605
<i>They praise my unmatched wisdom,</i>

519
00:39:57,313 --> 00:39:59,938
{\an8}<i>yet never see you behind me.</i>

520
00:40:00,896 --> 00:40:03,271
<i>The world I saw from your shoulders,</i>

521
00:40:03,855 --> 00:40:06,855
<i>I haven't learned to see any other way.</i>

522
00:40:08,396 --> 00:40:11,646
<i>Just because you did not nurse me,
must I not call you Mother?</i>

523
00:40:12,438 --> 00:40:15,688
<i>Is it not my sorrow to live in a language
too poor to understand what I feel?</i>

524
00:40:16,396 --> 00:40:18,480
<i>Be the star that guides my ship,</i>

525
00:40:20,021 --> 00:40:24,271
<i>and lead this little child of
yours, safe across the waters.</i>

526
00:40:26,105 --> 00:40:26,980
Ramappa!

527
00:40:27,855 --> 00:40:29,770
Don't move, you'll get cut.

528
00:40:29,771 --> 00:40:32,187
Will I get a big mustache like you?

529
00:40:32,188 --> 00:40:34,687
You'll get an even better mustache.

530
00:40:34,688 --> 00:40:35,563
Dad!

531
00:40:49,980 --> 00:40:51,813
When did you last see your father?

532
00:40:56,855 --> 00:40:59,438
- It's been five years.
- I could tell.

533
00:41:26,771 --> 00:41:27,938
Wake up, Your Highness.

534
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:32,438
The sun is out.

535
00:41:38,730 --> 00:41:39,896
Good morning, Appa.

536
00:41:43,230 --> 00:41:44,188
Achchamma!

537
00:41:44,813 --> 00:41:45,771
Good morning!

538
00:41:46,396 --> 00:41:48,771
How come I didn't see you yesterday?

539
00:41:53,105 --> 00:41:55,855
My late brother-in-law has a son, Appa.

540
00:41:56,938 --> 00:41:58,105
Two days ago,

541
00:41:58,521 --> 00:42:01,230
he decapitated my son.

542
00:42:02,730 --> 00:42:03,770
Yes, Appa.

543
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:05,229
In a fit of rage,

544
00:42:05,230 --> 00:42:10,230
my husband stormed out to kill him.
The nephew.

545
00:42:11,105 --> 00:42:14,520
Instead, the nephew
burned my husband alive!

546
00:42:14,521 --> 00:42:15,396
What?!

547
00:42:16,063 --> 00:42:17,480
Did no one stop him?

548
00:42:17,813 --> 00:42:18,937
What were you doing?

549
00:42:18,938 --> 00:42:20,855
No one stopped them.

550
00:42:21,105 --> 00:42:22,896
Instead, they cheered.

551
00:42:24,730 --> 00:42:26,896
But now that I think about it,

552
00:42:27,688 --> 00:42:29,563
I wasn't even in the dream.

553
00:42:30,188 --> 00:42:31,980
- Dream?
- Yes, Appa.

554
00:42:32,355 --> 00:42:34,980
I was frightened by that dream.

555
00:42:35,230 --> 00:42:37,229
So, although I knew you were coming,

556
00:42:37,230 --> 00:42:40,187
I went to seek help from
the saint in Thurakapalle.

557
00:42:40,188 --> 00:42:42,020
Enough of your stories!

558
00:42:42,021 --> 00:42:44,229
You start making things
up first thing in the morning.

559
00:42:44,230 --> 00:42:47,312
They're not stories.
I am telling it like it is.

560
00:42:47,313 --> 00:42:50,146
Yeah, yeah.
Go, get me a glass of ginger milk.

561
00:42:51,146 --> 00:42:53,188
You never believe anything I say.

562
00:42:53,438 --> 00:42:56,271
I'll share my worries
with Appa once you leave.

563
00:42:57,563 --> 00:42:59,105
Should I get you anything, Appa?

564
00:43:00,938 --> 00:43:01,896
Black coffee.

565
00:43:04,605 --> 00:43:05,521
Black coffee?

566
00:43:06,730 --> 00:43:07,646
Sure, Appa.

567
00:43:11,771 --> 00:43:12,980
Crazy woman.

568
00:43:19,771 --> 00:43:22,230
If you turn her stories into films,

569
00:43:22,563 --> 00:43:24,230
you'll make millions.

570
00:43:25,396 --> 00:43:27,230
Okay, look at me.

571
00:43:29,605 --> 00:43:31,896
Good. Open your mouth
and show your tongue.

572
00:43:32,355 --> 00:43:34,188
- Why?
- Do it, I'll tell you.

573
00:43:39,938 --> 00:43:41,021
I'm a doctor, right?

574
00:43:41,771 --> 00:43:45,438
I don't need to ask how you are.
I can see for myself.

575
00:43:46,271 --> 00:43:47,230
You are doing good.

576
00:43:47,521 --> 00:43:49,980
Hiding the truth even at this age,
are you?

577
00:43:54,105 --> 00:43:56,021
Oh! This is about your dad?

578
00:43:56,563 --> 00:43:58,520
I'll tell you. But first, get out of bed.

579
00:43:58,521 --> 00:43:59,980
You told him I was married?

580
00:44:01,730 --> 00:44:03,813
I'll tell you. Go freshen up first.

581
00:44:04,230 --> 00:44:05,355
We'll talk about it over a coffee.

582
00:44:15,938 --> 00:44:17,855
The new nurse who came
to care for Siddappa sir.

583
00:44:18,313 --> 00:44:19,230
Her name is Renuka.

584
00:44:20,230 --> 00:44:22,854
Shall we ask her if she knows?

585
00:44:22,855 --> 00:44:24,063
Yes. We can.

586
00:44:33,021 --> 00:44:33,896
Achchamma?

587
00:44:36,355 --> 00:44:38,687
Yes. How do you know?

588
00:44:38,688 --> 00:44:40,562
Everyone was saying that…

589
00:44:40,563 --> 00:44:42,896
the house wasn't the same
without Achchamma.

590
00:44:43,021 --> 00:44:44,895
When I saw that the house was glowing,

591
00:44:44,896 --> 00:44:46,271
I knew you were back.

592
00:44:46,896 --> 00:44:48,813
You're a smart lady!

593
00:44:50,313 --> 00:44:53,271
Thank you.
Since you're in charge of the house,

594
00:44:53,396 --> 00:44:55,855
they didn't even bother giving me a room.

595
00:44:57,646 --> 00:45:00,312
Could you arrange a room for me, madam?

596
00:45:00,313 --> 00:45:02,270
I will.

597
00:45:02,271 --> 00:45:04,438
But do you know how to make dark coffee?

598
00:45:05,438 --> 00:45:07,271
- Dark coffee?
- Yes, dark coffee.

599
00:45:10,146 --> 00:45:12,145
- Oh! Black coffee?
- Yes, black coffee!

600
00:45:12,146 --> 00:45:14,396
- Of course, I know!
- Then come with me.

601
00:45:15,313 --> 00:45:18,230
Here, this coffee is made with cow milk.

602
00:45:18,521 --> 00:45:20,063
This one is made with buffalo milk.

603
00:45:20,646 --> 00:45:22,146
This one has goat milk.

604
00:45:22,396 --> 00:45:23,980
And this one has donkey milk.

605
00:45:24,355 --> 00:45:27,688
No matter what milk I use,
the coffee just won't turn black.

606
00:45:37,563 --> 00:45:38,855
Girl, why are you laughing like that?

607
00:45:42,813 --> 00:45:44,355
Nothing. I'll tell you how.

608
00:45:44,730 --> 00:45:46,438
But you need to get me a nice room.

609
00:45:46,771 --> 00:45:49,312
Hey, silly, I'll treat you
like a queen. Just help me.

610
00:45:49,313 --> 00:45:52,271
Hey, be respectful. Don't call me silly.

611
00:45:54,105 --> 00:45:55,896
I'll treat you like a queen, madam.

612
00:45:56,688 --> 00:45:58,021
Please help me.

613
00:45:59,771 --> 00:46:01,313
Fine. Do you have the decoction?

614
00:46:03,646 --> 00:46:06,271
What color does milk turn
when you add decoction?

615
00:46:06,396 --> 00:46:08,438
I guess, a shade of yellow.

616
00:46:09,063 --> 00:46:10,229
What if we use water instead of milk?

617
00:46:10,230 --> 00:46:11,979
There will be no change in color.

618
00:46:11,980 --> 00:46:13,187
It'll remain black.

619
00:46:13,188 --> 00:46:16,063
Is milk the only way to get color?

620
00:46:16,313 --> 00:46:17,605
Isn't black a color in itself?

621
00:46:18,021 --> 00:46:20,105
With hot water, it'll be hot.

622
00:46:20,563 --> 00:46:22,729
And with sugar, it'll also be sweet.

623
00:46:22,730 --> 00:46:24,855
Simple. Black coffee is ready.

624
00:46:29,771 --> 00:46:34,230
When you renounced wealth
and family like Gautama Buddha,

625
00:46:35,063 --> 00:46:37,896
the lack of an heir to
carry on the Bhuvana line…

626
00:46:38,355 --> 00:46:39,980
has affected him a lot.

627
00:46:41,896 --> 00:46:44,396
Look, it's been six months.

628
00:46:45,480 --> 00:46:46,855
It's called a hemorrhagic stroke.

629
00:46:48,480 --> 00:46:50,063
We tried a lot of medications.

630
00:46:51,063 --> 00:46:52,021
Nothing helped.

631
00:46:53,105 --> 00:46:58,063
As a final resort, we even told him
you were married.

632
00:47:01,021 --> 00:47:02,355
Maybe it would've worked
if it were true.

633
00:47:03,938 --> 00:47:04,813
What?

634
00:47:05,480 --> 00:47:07,813
Are you trying to guilt-trip
me over his condition?

635
00:47:08,688 --> 00:47:11,313
Why so harsh? Why would I do that?

636
00:47:11,730 --> 00:47:12,605
Have a seat.

637
00:47:16,188 --> 00:47:17,355
If I had the chance,

638
00:47:17,855 --> 00:47:20,146
I would try to make you
understand one thing, Ramudu.

639
00:47:20,688 --> 00:47:21,645
What is it?

640
00:47:21,646 --> 00:47:25,813
Your dad shows no signs of improvement.

641
00:47:27,730 --> 00:47:30,313
There are many around you,
waiting for him to die,

642
00:47:31,105 --> 00:47:32,355
so they could steal this estate.

643
00:47:34,896 --> 00:47:36,896
For as long as he was alive,

644
00:47:37,063 --> 00:47:39,063
my dad waited to hand over things to you.

645
00:47:39,605 --> 00:47:41,188
Now that responsibility
hangs over my head.

646
00:47:42,855 --> 00:47:43,813
As long as he was alive?

647
00:47:44,855 --> 00:47:45,938
What happened to your father?

648
00:47:46,396 --> 00:47:47,438
It's been eight months.

649
00:47:48,271 --> 00:47:49,146
How?

650
00:47:50,146 --> 00:47:51,855
Almost the same situation.

651
00:47:53,021 --> 00:47:55,063
My wife and I had three children,
all daughters.

652
00:47:56,188 --> 00:47:58,396
"I need a grandson.
Try again," my father said.

653
00:47:58,855 --> 00:48:01,021
My wife couldn't.
And so she got sterilized.

654
00:48:03,021 --> 00:48:06,313
The pain of having no heir killed him.

655
00:48:07,646 --> 00:48:09,812
Even in the sixties,
people are so obsessed over

656
00:48:09,813 --> 00:48:13,437
caste, lineage, religion, and color.

657
00:48:13,438 --> 00:48:14,688
Not just the sixties.

658
00:48:15,355 --> 00:48:18,438
This will go on even in 2020.

659
00:48:19,146 --> 00:48:20,605
And not just in this country.

660
00:48:21,230 --> 00:48:22,896
It's the same situation
all around the world.

661
00:48:23,438 --> 00:48:24,896
We're only different in appearance.

662
00:48:25,605 --> 00:48:27,938
Deep down, all humans are alike.

663
00:48:28,438 --> 00:48:30,270
The world will heal
when people get this.

664
00:48:30,271 --> 00:48:31,521
That is impossible.

665
00:48:32,355 --> 00:48:36,438
Because all humans share a mental flaw.

666
00:48:36,813 --> 00:48:41,146
We look at what is visible to us
and believe that's the truth.

667
00:48:41,521 --> 00:48:45,605
Just as we believe the sun rises
in the east and sets in the west.

668
00:48:46,021 --> 00:48:47,480
The truth is,

669
00:48:47,688 --> 00:48:49,520
the day man started to walk
on his two feet

670
00:48:49,521 --> 00:48:53,146
and migrated to various places,
the human race became one mixed pot.

671
00:48:54,188 --> 00:48:57,229
But we divide ourselves as black or white,

672
00:48:57,230 --> 00:49:01,270
tall or short, fat or thin,
Muslim or Christian.

673
00:49:01,271 --> 00:49:03,521
You're a Kshatriya, and I'm a Brahman.
And that is all people see.

674
00:49:04,063 --> 00:49:05,730
Caste also matters, you say?

675
00:49:05,938 --> 00:49:06,813
Of course.

676
00:49:07,438 --> 00:49:10,896
Which is why I wear my holy thread
and you wear your turban.

677
00:49:14,188 --> 00:49:17,021
You said exactly what I wanted to hear.

678
00:49:18,855 --> 00:49:20,480
You know which nerve to hit, don't you?

679
00:49:20,771 --> 00:49:23,105
Each disease needs its own cure, right?

680
00:49:24,188 --> 00:49:26,355
I'm a doctor. Old habits die hard.

681
00:49:27,188 --> 00:49:29,188
They claimed democracy 20 years ago.

682
00:49:30,396 --> 00:49:31,313
What do you say about that?

683
00:49:32,021 --> 00:49:33,438
Remember, only what I want to hear.

684
00:49:33,563 --> 00:49:34,896
What democracy?

685
00:49:36,646 --> 00:49:40,146
As long as we glorify the
tales of Kings to children,

686
00:49:40,938 --> 00:49:42,438
this country won't be a democracy.

687
00:49:43,896 --> 00:49:45,105
Don't include me in this.

688
00:49:45,896 --> 00:49:47,396
- I'm different.
- Oh, no.

689
00:49:47,855 --> 00:49:49,063
No one is different.

690
00:49:49,896 --> 00:49:52,355
It's just that you're not
socially conditioned yet.

691
00:49:52,688 --> 00:49:53,605
That is it.

692
00:49:54,146 --> 00:49:55,813
Once that happens,

693
00:49:55,938 --> 00:49:57,896
you can finally become one of us.

694
00:49:58,188 --> 00:50:00,230
- Good morning, doctor.
- Good morning.

695
00:50:00,938 --> 00:50:02,105
She's Renuka.

696
00:50:03,980 --> 00:50:04,938
An Anglo Indian.

697
00:50:05,396 --> 00:50:07,271
She was born and raised
in an orphanage.

698
00:50:07,855 --> 00:50:09,021
She's a nurse at my hospital.

699
00:50:09,230 --> 00:50:11,105
We've already been introduced, doctor.

700
00:50:11,313 --> 00:50:12,271
Here.

701
00:50:12,688 --> 00:50:13,605
This is for you.

702
00:50:15,146 --> 00:50:16,021
This is for you.

703
00:50:16,688 --> 00:50:19,105
Why are you serving us?
Where's Achchamma?

704
00:50:20,188 --> 00:50:22,313
Achchamma is way too busy.

705
00:50:22,688 --> 00:50:24,354
She said the doctor was here.

706
00:50:24,355 --> 00:50:26,105
So I thought I'd bring these and meet him.

707
00:50:26,688 --> 00:50:28,396
- Thank you.
- How do you like it here, Renuka?

708
00:50:28,730 --> 00:50:29,938
It's great, doctor.

709
00:50:30,480 --> 00:50:32,521
This house.
The trees that surround it.

710
00:50:33,146 --> 00:50:34,396
I feel like settling here.

711
00:50:34,730 --> 00:50:35,730
I knew you would like it.

712
00:50:36,271 --> 00:50:37,938
Are you recording Mr. Siddappa's vitals?

713
00:50:38,230 --> 00:50:39,230
I am, doctor.

714
00:50:39,438 --> 00:50:40,521
Everything is normal.

715
00:50:40,730 --> 00:50:43,605
But his blood pressure is quite high.

716
00:50:43,813 --> 00:50:45,520
For a person in a coma,

717
00:50:45,521 --> 00:50:47,480
it is rare to have blood
pressure this high.

718
00:50:47,855 --> 00:50:48,771
Okay.

719
00:50:49,271 --> 00:50:50,271
I'll come and check.

720
00:50:50,813 --> 00:50:52,021
Let me see your palm.

721
00:50:52,605 --> 00:50:55,146
- What for?
- I'll tell you. Just show me once.

722
00:50:55,688 --> 00:50:56,563
Your right palm.

723
00:51:00,438 --> 00:51:02,729
Ah! See that lifeline?

724
00:51:02,730 --> 00:51:05,938
It's short from all that cigar smoking.

725
00:51:06,271 --> 00:51:07,438
I don't have such habits.

726
00:51:07,563 --> 00:51:10,520
Look at mine. It reaches my index finger.

727
00:51:10,521 --> 00:51:11,438
Hey, Renuka!

728
00:51:11,938 --> 00:51:13,230
- What's this?
- Hold on.

729
00:51:15,396 --> 00:51:16,354
She's right.

730
00:51:16,355 --> 00:51:17,896
Hey Achari, show me your hand.

731
00:51:18,146 --> 00:51:19,896
Oh please.
Why are you playing along?

732
00:51:20,605 --> 00:51:21,480
Show me.

733
00:51:24,730 --> 00:51:25,605
She's right.

734
00:51:26,188 --> 00:51:27,521
His line is long too.

735
00:51:28,188 --> 00:51:29,438
But see my line.

736
00:51:29,938 --> 00:51:31,646
It's short. But it's thick.

737
00:51:31,980 --> 00:51:32,855
Which means…

738
00:51:33,063 --> 00:51:35,438
I will live multiple lives in one.

739
00:51:36,396 --> 00:51:37,271
Look at yours.

740
00:51:37,605 --> 00:51:39,771
They start out thick but end up thin.

741
00:51:40,521 --> 00:51:42,730
Meaning, your lives…

742
00:51:46,021 --> 00:51:47,730
Yeah! Let me see yours.

743
00:52:00,438 --> 00:52:01,980
Yes, doctor.
You called for me?

744
00:52:03,146 --> 00:52:04,021
Yeah.

745
00:52:05,605 --> 00:52:06,563
What was all that?

746
00:52:07,438 --> 00:52:08,938
Know your place.

747
00:52:10,355 --> 00:52:12,188
Is it wrong to be myself, doctor?

748
00:52:14,063 --> 00:52:15,855
There's no need to be
yourself with everyone.

749
00:52:16,855 --> 00:52:18,396
You'd do well to know your place.

750
00:52:20,105 --> 00:52:22,521
I sent you here because you were
being too playful at the hospital.

751
00:52:24,188 --> 00:52:25,355
Try to be in your limits.

752
00:52:26,230 --> 00:52:27,146
Let's go.

753
00:52:32,521 --> 00:52:34,688
He couldn't say that respectfully?

754
00:52:35,771 --> 00:52:36,896
I'll be myself.

755
00:52:40,188 --> 00:52:41,896
If they don't like me, it's their problem.

756
00:52:50,896 --> 00:52:52,063
THE SONG OF MY LAND

757
00:53:19,355 --> 00:53:22,563
What song is this, Dad?
You keep playing it.

758
00:53:25,271 --> 00:53:28,021
Your mother lives in this song, Ramappa.

759
00:53:29,146 --> 00:53:30,438
That's why I keep playing it.

760
00:53:31,730 --> 00:53:33,688
It's the song I dedicate to my Vasudha.

761
00:53:42,646 --> 00:53:48,396
Just as a golden Bougainville creeper,

762
00:53:48,896 --> 00:53:53,188
she lured me.

763
00:53:53,646 --> 00:53:58,396
She's the young woman of the ages.

764
00:53:58,688 --> 00:54:03,105
I adore your eyes.

765
00:54:03,521 --> 00:54:08,313
Like a star in the sky,

766
00:54:08,521 --> 00:54:13,230
she moves like a bright streak.

767
00:54:13,521 --> 00:54:17,980
As I look at her face,

768
00:54:18,355 --> 00:54:23,230
confusions arise within.

769
00:54:23,396 --> 00:54:28,105
I, a wanderer, who's
always on the move,

770
00:54:28,438 --> 00:54:33,146
take command and lock me up

771
00:54:33,480 --> 00:54:38,146
with those eyes,

772
00:54:38,521 --> 00:54:42,938
my love.

773
00:54:43,438 --> 00:54:48,146
I can never leave,

774
00:54:48,480 --> 00:54:53,230
even if you ask.

775
00:55:14,271 --> 00:55:15,646
- Hello.
- Hi.

776
00:55:16,188 --> 00:55:18,021
I'm going to the town.
Would you like to join me?

777
00:55:18,730 --> 00:55:21,729
Sorry, I don't feel up to it today.

778
00:55:21,730 --> 00:55:23,230
Oh no, what's wrong?

779
00:55:23,646 --> 00:55:25,271
- Is everything alright?
- Yeah.

780
00:55:26,063 --> 00:55:27,980
- It's a bit personal.
- Oh.

781
00:55:31,188 --> 00:55:32,646
- Take care.
- Thank you.

782
00:55:35,271 --> 00:55:36,188
Hey!

783
00:55:36,521 --> 00:55:37,396
Girl!

784
00:55:37,771 --> 00:55:38,646
Girl!

785
00:55:38,855 --> 00:55:40,854
That's a wild horse.
It can't be controlled.

786
00:55:40,855 --> 00:55:41,855
I'll get you another.

787
00:55:42,063 --> 00:55:43,355
So what if it's wild?

788
00:55:44,105 --> 00:55:46,021
It'll have to be tamed at some point.

789
00:55:46,855 --> 00:55:48,313
Girl! Girl!

790
00:55:53,730 --> 00:55:54,646
Careful!

791
00:56:00,646 --> 00:56:02,855
Oh no! Oh!

792
00:56:03,480 --> 00:56:04,438
I told you.

793
00:56:05,855 --> 00:56:07,355
Look, you hurt yourself!

794
00:56:12,813 --> 00:56:15,396
Don't we hurt ourselves
while learning to ride a bicycle?

795
00:56:15,688 --> 00:56:16,605
This is the same.

796
00:56:21,521 --> 00:56:23,063
I'll deal with you later.

797
00:56:25,105 --> 00:56:28,105
I was searching for something.

798
00:56:29,730 --> 00:56:34,480
I understand what I need now.

799
00:56:35,188 --> 00:56:38,396
I struggle with loneliness.

800
00:56:39,813 --> 00:56:44,480
I understood what
that desperation was.

801
00:56:45,271 --> 00:56:48,229
- That's what I said.
- I stand by you,

802
00:56:48,230 --> 00:56:50,312
I totally lost track of time.
I need to give him saline.

803
00:56:50,313 --> 00:56:55,270
my manhood found its purpose.

804
00:56:55,271 --> 00:56:59,480
The moment your fragrance hits me,

805
00:57:00,021 --> 00:57:04,396
my pride bowed down.

806
00:57:04,813 --> 00:57:09,563
Any warrior

807
00:57:09,855 --> 00:57:14,521
will become a slave

808
00:57:14,771 --> 00:57:18,938
when he looks at her face,

809
00:57:19,730 --> 00:57:24,937
confusions arise within.

810
00:57:24,938 --> 00:57:31,855
I, a wanderer, who's
always on the move,

811
00:57:32,230 --> 00:57:34,563
take command and lock me up

812
00:57:34,855 --> 00:57:39,563
with those eyes,

813
00:57:39,938 --> 00:57:44,271
my love.

814
00:57:44,813 --> 00:57:49,438
I can never leave,

815
00:57:49,896 --> 00:57:54,688
even if you ask.

816
00:57:57,271 --> 00:57:59,521
Hey! There's a pond in your estate?

817
00:58:00,188 --> 00:58:03,521
That pond is very dear to my parents.

818
00:58:04,855 --> 00:58:06,605
My mother died giving birth to me.

819
00:58:07,730 --> 00:58:12,396
Ever since, my father
has come here in her memory.

820
00:58:12,605 --> 00:58:15,605
Your father loves
you and your mother a lot.

821
00:58:16,355 --> 00:58:17,271
How do you know?

822
00:58:26,688 --> 00:58:29,063
Mr. Ramappa! Mr. Ramappa!

823
00:58:31,230 --> 00:58:32,188
What happened?

824
00:58:34,480 --> 00:58:35,438
Nothing.

825
00:58:36,021 --> 00:58:37,980
Okay, shall we go to the pond?

826
00:58:38,855 --> 00:58:41,355
Woah! The pond? Why?

827
00:58:41,688 --> 00:58:43,355
I'm quite fond of water.

828
00:58:43,605 --> 00:58:46,729
I just want to feel what it's
like to stand in the middle of it.

829
00:58:46,730 --> 00:58:48,771
Then, you go ahead.
I'll stay right here.

830
00:58:48,980 --> 00:58:51,480
Why so? Why won't you come?

831
00:58:52,980 --> 00:58:53,896
Well…

832
00:58:55,521 --> 00:58:56,605
I'm afraid of water.

833
00:59:02,980 --> 00:59:04,771
Really? You're afraid of water?

834
00:59:06,063 --> 00:59:07,021
Why are you laughing?

835
00:59:07,730 --> 00:59:09,480
Because I'm afraid of water?

836
00:59:10,313 --> 00:59:11,188
Why?

837
00:59:11,313 --> 00:59:13,188
Aren't men allowed to have fears?

838
00:59:13,646 --> 00:59:14,563
I didn't mean that.

839
00:59:14,730 --> 00:59:16,813
- What's your name?
- Ramappa.

840
00:59:17,146 --> 00:59:18,730
No, your full name.

841
00:59:19,813 --> 00:59:21,688
Bhuvanam Ramappa Rao Bahadur.

842
00:59:22,063 --> 00:59:24,271
You know what Rao Bahadur means, right?

843
00:59:25,021 --> 00:59:29,271
Rao Bahadur is the title
the British gave my grandfather.

844
00:59:29,813 --> 00:59:31,771
We've all carried that name ever since.

845
00:59:32,105 --> 00:59:34,021
We humans are so strange, aren't we?

846
00:59:34,313 --> 00:59:38,271
People name their children not knowing
who they'll grow up to be.

847
00:59:39,271 --> 00:59:40,813
'Rao' means prince.

848
00:59:41,313 --> 00:59:43,063
And 'Bahadur' means brave.

849
00:59:43,396 --> 00:59:46,855
'Rao Bahadur' means 'a brave prince'.

850
00:59:48,105 --> 00:59:50,521
And look at you, afraid
to step into the water.

851
00:59:51,063 --> 00:59:53,480
Fine, you stay here, and I'll go.

852
01:00:57,980 --> 01:00:59,438
Mr. Ramappa!

853
01:01:00,063 --> 01:01:03,396
The world seems so beautiful from here!

854
01:01:07,105 --> 01:01:09,938
There's bliss in these babbling waters!

855
01:01:11,813 --> 01:01:14,145
This wind makes me feel as though

856
01:01:14,146 --> 01:01:16,355
my soul flew out of my
body and spoke to me.

857
01:01:19,813 --> 01:01:24,188
Now I understand why this place
meant so much to your parents.

858
01:01:25,896 --> 01:01:30,438
O you charming beauty,

859
01:01:30,646 --> 01:01:35,938
as my heart looks at you,

860
01:01:36,396 --> 01:01:41,688
peace hits me

861
01:01:42,188 --> 01:01:46,563
like a wave.

862
01:01:56,271 --> 01:01:58,730
- Hello.
- I want to show you a secret. Come.

863
01:02:10,105 --> 01:02:10,980
Come on in.

864
01:02:19,771 --> 01:02:20,813
Do you see that hand?

865
01:02:22,146 --> 01:02:23,104
I do.

866
01:02:23,105 --> 01:02:24,021
Come with me.

867
01:02:28,646 --> 01:02:30,271
Let's check again in half an hour.

868
01:02:30,896 --> 01:02:31,771
Okay.

869
01:02:45,521 --> 01:02:46,438
Now look!

870
01:02:47,188 --> 01:02:48,146
Yeah, it…

871
01:02:50,146 --> 01:02:52,854
- What?!
- See? Isn't it interesting?

872
01:02:52,855 --> 01:02:54,938
Put it back.
Let me see it again.

873
01:03:01,855 --> 01:03:03,355
- Let's go. We'll be back.
- No, no, no.

874
01:03:03,771 --> 01:03:04,730
I want to see it happen.

875
01:03:05,063 --> 01:03:08,021
It doesn't work that way.
I've tried many times.

876
01:03:08,188 --> 01:03:09,605
We'll have to leave the room.

877
01:03:16,896 --> 01:03:18,521
Wait, don't pull.

878
01:03:21,730 --> 01:03:22,730
It's back!

879
01:03:23,730 --> 01:03:26,813
Exactly! It's the secret of
the home of the Bhuvanas.

880
01:03:27,438 --> 01:03:28,521
How's it even possible?

881
01:03:28,938 --> 01:03:30,021
I'll tell you. Come.

882
01:03:33,188 --> 01:03:36,145
Look at your ancestors' paintings.

883
01:03:36,146 --> 01:03:38,146
They all have their
right hand on their chest.

884
01:03:38,313 --> 01:03:40,437
I've read the histories of many kings.

885
01:03:40,438 --> 01:03:42,145
They all do it as a mark of pride.

886
01:03:42,146 --> 01:03:43,021
There, look.

887
01:03:43,146 --> 01:03:46,896
All of them put their hand on their chest.

888
01:03:47,105 --> 01:03:50,230
That's why, even in a coma,
he didn't lose this habit.

889
01:03:50,480 --> 01:03:53,521
They say once pride takes hold,
it lasts till death.

890
01:03:54,355 --> 01:03:56,480
No, no. Don't get me wrong.

891
01:03:57,063 --> 01:03:58,605
It's just a saying.

892
01:04:01,980 --> 01:04:03,938
You've been all over the world.

893
01:04:04,230 --> 01:04:07,813
But you haven't noticed
what runs in your family.

894
01:04:31,355 --> 01:04:32,271
Appa?

895
01:04:33,396 --> 01:04:34,271
Appa?

896
01:04:35,396 --> 01:04:36,271
Appa!

897
01:04:44,563 --> 01:04:45,480
Achchamma?

898
01:04:46,355 --> 01:04:47,355
What are you doing here?

899
01:04:49,605 --> 01:04:50,730
Wasn't Renuka here?

900
01:04:52,396 --> 01:04:53,480
What is this, Appa?

901
01:04:54,313 --> 01:04:57,105
You've been chanting
her name for a month.

902
01:04:57,563 --> 01:04:58,770
Why would she still be here?

903
01:04:58,771 --> 01:05:02,271
She left right after your father died.

904
01:05:08,855 --> 01:05:09,771
Yeah.

905
01:05:11,938 --> 01:05:13,063
She left, didn't she?

906
01:05:24,605 --> 01:05:25,480
Yes?

907
01:05:26,021 --> 01:05:27,230
I need to have a word with you.

908
01:05:27,396 --> 01:05:28,313
About what?

909
01:05:29,146 --> 01:05:31,646
Not here. In private.

910
01:05:32,396 --> 01:05:34,105
Okay, where shall we talk then?

911
01:06:06,563 --> 01:06:08,813
I'll miss this pond a lot.

912
01:06:10,813 --> 01:06:13,063
So, what is it you wanted to say?

913
01:06:17,855 --> 01:06:20,355
I never thought
I'd come back to this home.

914
01:06:22,230 --> 01:06:23,230
But I did.

915
01:06:26,396 --> 01:06:27,896
Maybe it was just to meet you.

916
01:06:29,563 --> 01:06:31,855
I've never had the desire to marry.

917
01:06:32,938 --> 01:06:34,230
But since I met you…

918
01:06:35,313 --> 01:06:37,021
and spent all this time with you,

919
01:06:38,605 --> 01:06:39,896
I had a change of heart.

920
01:06:45,105 --> 01:06:46,230
I like you.

921
01:06:47,813 --> 01:06:49,146
If you like me too,

922
01:06:50,688 --> 01:06:52,563
I'd like to marry you.

923
01:06:53,730 --> 01:06:54,646
Oh no.

924
01:06:55,146 --> 01:06:58,438
If I led you on,

925
01:06:59,688 --> 01:07:00,813
I'm really sorry.

926
01:07:02,438 --> 01:07:05,563
I never had such feelings for you.

927
01:07:07,271 --> 01:07:11,980
Also, I'm in love with someone else.

928
01:07:13,855 --> 01:07:14,896
So,

929
01:07:16,021 --> 01:07:18,063
it's a no.

930
01:07:25,146 --> 01:07:26,021
Water.

931
01:07:26,813 --> 01:07:27,730
Water.

932
01:07:29,938 --> 01:07:30,855
Water.

933
01:07:31,896 --> 01:07:33,563
Water! Water!

934
01:07:36,313 --> 01:07:37,980
Water! Water!

935
01:07:39,438 --> 01:07:40,896
Water! Water!

936
01:07:41,438 --> 01:07:42,355
Water!

937
01:07:42,521 --> 01:07:44,230
- Water! Water!
- What happened?

938
01:07:44,563 --> 01:07:45,771
Water! Water!

939
01:07:45,980 --> 01:07:47,188
I want to leave!

940
01:07:51,063 --> 01:07:52,605
I want to get to the shore!

941
01:07:53,396 --> 01:07:55,313
I want to get to the shore!

942
01:07:55,813 --> 01:07:57,312
- Mr. Ramappa!
- Shore!

943
01:07:57,313 --> 01:08:00,063
We're almost there. Don't worry.

944
01:08:00,646 --> 01:08:05,146
I want to get to the shore!

945
01:08:06,605 --> 01:08:08,480
I want to get to the shore!

946
01:08:54,188 --> 01:08:55,105
Appa?

947
01:08:56,271 --> 01:08:57,188
Appa!

948
01:08:57,980 --> 01:09:02,105
- Why do you drift off these days, Appa?
- What is it?

949
01:09:02,271 --> 01:09:04,896
Everything's set for
your journey tomorrow.

950
01:09:05,438 --> 01:09:08,605
Mr. Achari will send a taxi by 9 AM.

951
01:09:10,271 --> 01:09:11,230
Taxi?

952
01:09:12,271 --> 01:09:13,312
What happened to our cars?

953
01:09:13,313 --> 01:09:15,521
There are no drivers available.

954
01:09:15,730 --> 01:09:16,938
Where did they all go?

955
01:09:17,396 --> 01:09:18,688
Your father passed away.

956
01:09:20,396 --> 01:09:22,396
Now, you're leaving too.

957
01:09:23,646 --> 01:09:25,896
There is no work here.

958
01:09:26,896 --> 01:09:28,605
So, they're looking for new Masters.

959
01:10:41,021 --> 01:10:42,063
Ramappa!

960
01:11:07,730 --> 01:11:09,188
What was so pressing up here?

961
01:11:10,646 --> 01:11:13,437
You passed away
before getting him married.

962
01:11:13,438 --> 01:11:15,146
I wasn't dying to be here.

963
01:11:15,896 --> 01:11:17,979
I went through hell for 5 years
before getting here.

964
01:11:17,980 --> 01:11:18,855
Enough!

965
01:11:19,855 --> 01:11:21,604
He talks as if only he went through hell

966
01:11:21,605 --> 01:11:22,980
and all of us went up to heaven.

967
01:11:24,521 --> 01:11:26,230
Raising a kid won't cut it!

968
01:11:26,521 --> 01:11:28,521
You need to condition him with our norms.

969
01:11:29,313 --> 01:11:30,230
And you?

970
01:11:30,938 --> 01:11:32,480
Please don't involve me in this.

971
01:11:35,938 --> 01:11:37,063
Were you even listening?

972
01:11:38,021 --> 01:11:40,062
He's leaving tomorrow!

973
01:11:40,063 --> 01:11:42,938
Who will take my lineage forward?

974
01:11:52,480 --> 01:11:54,188
There we go. He's up.

975
01:11:55,313 --> 01:11:56,188
Ask him yourself.

976
01:12:11,646 --> 01:12:14,063
- Who are you all?
- It's us, Ramappa.

977
01:12:15,146 --> 01:12:16,438
Your ancestors.

978
01:12:17,313 --> 01:12:19,688
The ones from the paintings
all around this house.

979
01:12:20,146 --> 01:12:21,063
Don't you recognize us?

980
01:12:24,521 --> 01:12:25,562
Why are you here?

981
01:12:25,563 --> 01:12:27,605
It's nothing, my great
great great grandson.

982
01:12:28,730 --> 01:12:31,396
They say the crop thins
as the herd grows.

983
01:12:32,188 --> 01:12:35,771
But in my clan, it's the weak seeds
that made the herd decline.

984
01:12:36,271 --> 01:12:37,146
So?

985
01:12:37,563 --> 01:12:40,146
We heard you left home when your father

986
01:12:40,396 --> 01:12:41,480
asked you to marry and have children.

987
01:12:43,563 --> 01:12:46,021
- The world is my home.
- Shut up!

988
01:12:47,146 --> 01:12:49,105
To hell with the world!

989
01:12:49,688 --> 01:12:50,770
Army of heirs!

990
01:12:50,771 --> 01:12:51,813
Yes grandpa!

991
01:12:51,980 --> 01:12:55,188
His brain is completely muddled.

992
01:12:55,521 --> 01:12:59,438
Wash his brain and condition it
with societal norms.

993
01:12:59,771 --> 01:13:00,771
Bring him along!

994
01:13:13,271 --> 01:13:17,521
<i>The greatest of grandfathers is here.</i>

995
01:13:17,813 --> 01:13:22,855
<i>To rectify his fate.</i>

996
01:13:23,813 --> 01:13:29,145
<i>Obey me and</i>

997
01:13:29,146 --> 01:13:33,855
<i>Place your head here, o grandson!</i>

998
01:13:48,188 --> 01:13:52,020
Woah! Grandpa, it looks very fresh.

999
01:13:52,021 --> 01:13:53,521
Just like a caveman.

1000
01:13:55,230 --> 01:13:56,270
Begin!

1001
01:13:56,271 --> 01:13:58,812
<i>I will enter the brain.</i>

1002
01:13:58,813 --> 01:14:01,229
<i>I will wreak havoc.</i>

1003
01:14:01,230 --> 01:14:05,896
<i>I will wash and clean it up.</i>

1004
01:14:06,396 --> 01:14:08,937
<i>I will scramble it.</i>

1005
01:14:08,938 --> 01:14:11,479
<i>I will chase the demon away.</i>

1006
01:14:11,480 --> 01:14:16,562
<i>I will inject ancestral ego
into your veins.</i>

1007
01:14:16,563 --> 01:14:18,979
<i>I will remind you of our pride.</i>

1008
01:14:18,980 --> 01:14:21,229
<i>Conditioning. Conditioning.</i>

1009
01:14:21,230 --> 01:14:24,020
<i>I will pour my rules all over.</i>

1010
01:14:24,021 --> 01:14:26,312
<i>Conditioning. Conditioning.</i>

1011
01:14:26,313 --> 01:14:29,145
<i>Learn your stature, o prince.</i>

1012
01:14:29,146 --> 01:14:31,354
<i>Sit on the throne,
rule without any doubt.</i>

1013
01:14:31,355 --> 01:14:33,104
<i>Twist your mustache.</i>

1014
01:14:33,105 --> 01:14:33,980
<i>Conditioning.</i>

1015
01:14:34,105 --> 01:14:35,604
<i>Show your rage.</i>

1016
01:14:35,605 --> 01:14:36,812
<i>Conditioning.</i>

1017
01:14:36,813 --> 01:14:40,313
<i>Power is a boon.</i>

1018
01:14:41,688 --> 01:14:46,812
<i>It was showered on you.</i>

1019
01:14:46,813 --> 01:14:50,271
<i>You must change your ways.</i>

1020
01:14:51,480 --> 01:14:56,646
<i>All your obstacles must be removed.</i>

1021
01:15:32,355 --> 01:15:34,937
<i>By hook or by crook,</i>

1022
01:15:34,938 --> 01:15:37,271
<i>I will fill you with the knowledge
of a thousand years.</i>

1023
01:15:37,438 --> 01:15:40,062
<i>Without any distractions
or forgetting traditions,</i>

1024
01:15:40,063 --> 01:15:42,562
<i>I will teach you the
ways of the kings.</i>

1025
01:15:42,563 --> 01:15:44,979
<i>So you won't compare
the good and the bad,</i>

1026
01:15:44,980 --> 01:15:47,520
<i>I shall mask your mind.</i>

1027
01:15:47,521 --> 01:15:50,020
<i>So the righteous truth
never reaches you,</i>

1028
01:15:50,021 --> 01:15:52,729
<i>I shall suffocate
you with intoxication.</i>

1029
01:15:52,730 --> 01:15:55,104
<i>Your idea of everyone being equal,</i>

1030
01:15:55,105 --> 01:15:57,645
<i>I shall wash it away tonight.</i>

1031
01:15:57,646 --> 01:15:59,938
<i>"What is mine, is only mine."</i>

1032
01:16:00,146 --> 01:16:02,771
<i>I shall fill it in every
inch of your body.</i>

1033
01:16:17,896 --> 01:16:21,355
<i>You are a king of all the land.</i>

1034
01:16:22,938 --> 01:16:26,563
<i>The people are slaves.</i>

1035
01:16:27,938 --> 01:16:33,062
<i>No one compares to you.</i>

1036
01:16:33,063 --> 01:16:35,604
<i>Do not forget this truth.</i>

1037
01:16:35,605 --> 01:16:38,438
<i>Wear this ancestral
pride on your head.</i>

1038
01:16:39,021 --> 01:16:41,937
<i>I will obey your norms.</i>

1039
01:16:41,938 --> 01:16:44,104
<i>Conditioning. Conditioning.</i>

1040
01:16:44,105 --> 01:16:46,812
<i>I will be the best of the best men.</i>

1041
01:16:46,813 --> 01:16:49,104
<i>Conditioning. Conditioning.</i>

1042
01:16:49,105 --> 01:16:51,979
<i>I now know my stature.</i>

1043
01:16:51,980 --> 01:16:54,145
<i>I will sit on the throne and
rule without a doubt.</i>

1044
01:16:54,146 --> 01:16:55,771
<i>I will twist my mustache.</i>

1045
01:16:56,021 --> 01:16:56,938
<i>Conditioning.</i>

1046
01:16:57,063 --> 01:16:59,312
<i>- I will show my rage.
- Conditioning.</i>

1047
01:16:59,313 --> 01:17:01,812
<i>Protect this knowledge as an asset.</i>

1048
01:17:01,813 --> 01:17:04,354
<i>Tend to it as a legacy.</i>

1049
01:17:04,355 --> 01:17:06,104
<i>For your lineage to continue.</i>

1050
01:17:06,105 --> 01:17:07,145
<i>Conditioning.</i>

1051
01:17:07,146 --> 01:17:10,021
<i>Forever!</i>

1052
01:17:42,688 --> 01:17:44,480
Appa must be here.
Come quickly.

1053
01:18:28,730 --> 01:18:29,896
How do I look, Achchamma?

1054
01:18:35,730 --> 01:18:37,146
You look like a king, Appa.

1055
01:18:38,105 --> 01:18:39,855
'Like a King'?

1056
01:18:40,480 --> 01:18:41,563
I am the king!

1057
01:18:53,230 --> 01:18:54,646
Can you drive a big car?

1058
01:19:28,563 --> 01:19:30,438
Excuse me! Who are you, sir?

1059
01:19:53,563 --> 01:19:54,480
Open your mouth.

1060
01:20:09,396 --> 01:20:10,271
Ramudu?

1061
01:20:11,396 --> 01:20:12,729
What's with the costume?

1062
01:20:12,730 --> 01:20:14,730
It's not a costume. It's a royal identity.

1063
01:20:15,188 --> 01:20:16,480
Royalty is in my blood.

1064
01:20:17,146 --> 01:20:18,271
You won't get it.

1065
01:20:19,980 --> 01:20:21,896
- Where's Renuka?
- Renuka?

1066
01:20:22,896 --> 01:20:23,771
Why?

1067
01:20:24,063 --> 01:20:25,980
Call her in. I have some work with her.

1068
01:20:26,438 --> 01:20:27,604
{\an8}Renuka is not here anymore.

1069
01:20:27,605 --> 01:20:29,145
{\an8}DR. NARAYANACHARI

1070
01:20:29,146 --> 01:20:30,063
{\an8}I fired her.

1071
01:20:31,230 --> 01:20:33,604
You fired her? Why?

1072
01:20:33,605 --> 01:20:36,355
Because she refused
to follow instructions.

1073
01:20:36,563 --> 01:20:37,480
That's why.

1074
01:20:38,646 --> 01:20:39,771
But why do you want her now?

1075
01:20:40,355 --> 01:20:43,230
- I want to marry her.
- What?

1076
01:20:44,355 --> 01:20:45,730
Am I hearing this right?

1077
01:20:46,480 --> 01:20:48,146
How can you marry her?

1078
01:20:48,271 --> 01:20:50,271
Why? What's wrong in it?

1079
01:20:50,688 --> 01:20:52,771
How does her stature compare to yours?

1080
01:20:55,105 --> 01:20:57,187
As a clerk's son who
married into wealth…

1081
01:20:57,188 --> 01:21:01,188
and built a hospital
on dowry money,

1082
01:21:01,688 --> 01:21:04,188
this talk of stature is
quite rich coming from you.

1083
01:21:05,730 --> 01:21:07,813
Stature is for men.
Leave women out of it.

1084
01:21:08,271 --> 01:21:09,646
They can just focus on femininity.

1085
01:21:10,063 --> 01:21:11,062
Ramudu?

1086
01:21:11,063 --> 01:21:12,480
Is it really you?

1087
01:21:12,938 --> 01:21:14,021
What happened to you?

1088
01:21:14,355 --> 01:21:17,437
Head split open, brain washed,
polished, and stitched with gold thread.

1089
01:21:17,438 --> 01:21:19,521
Woah, a lot has happened.

1090
01:21:20,105 --> 01:21:22,021
Anyway, I don't have
time to chat with you.

1091
01:21:22,146 --> 01:21:23,230
I need to produce heirs.

1092
01:21:23,813 --> 01:21:26,438
I want you to find her and
convince her to marry me.

1093
01:21:26,938 --> 01:21:28,271
If you don't…

1094
01:21:31,063 --> 01:21:34,771
People will lose their minds
trying to learn whose son is who.

1095
01:22:04,771 --> 01:22:06,063
I…

1096
01:22:06,730 --> 01:22:08,730
I've been very delusional lately.

1097
01:22:09,438 --> 01:22:11,146
I didn't take Achari seriously.

1098
01:22:11,646 --> 01:22:13,313
I need to see that doctor immediately.

1099
01:22:27,188 --> 01:22:29,230
Why did you call for me so early again?

1100
01:22:29,396 --> 01:22:31,230
A lot has happened, sir.

1101
01:22:33,813 --> 01:22:34,771
Where is Lavana?

1102
01:22:34,938 --> 01:22:36,771
Lavana sir is down with a fever.

1103
01:22:37,855 --> 01:22:38,730
Fever?

1104
01:22:39,313 --> 01:22:40,188
What happened?

1105
01:22:40,896 --> 01:22:43,771
Appa's madness has gotten worse, sir.

1106
01:22:44,271 --> 01:22:47,563
- He's been wreaking havoc all week.
- What happened?

1107
01:22:49,105 --> 01:22:51,105
What can I tell you, sir?

1108
01:22:51,813 --> 01:22:53,105
What do you mean?

1109
01:22:53,271 --> 01:22:56,646
- You said he wreaked havoc.
- Yeah, just listen.

1110
01:22:57,188 --> 01:23:00,188
The day after your last visit,

1111
01:23:00,313 --> 01:23:02,521
I gave him Kusuma's room key,
as he asked.

1112
01:23:02,688 --> 01:23:04,729
Kusuma's room key? Why?

1113
01:23:04,730 --> 01:23:06,812
I had no idea then.

1114
01:23:06,813 --> 01:23:08,479
But after a while,

1115
01:23:08,480 --> 01:23:11,188
he locked Renuka ma'am in that room,

1116
01:23:11,396 --> 01:23:13,730
and stormed around the house, shouting.

1117
01:23:17,230 --> 01:23:18,230
What are you saying?

1118
01:23:20,230 --> 01:23:21,230
She stepped out?

1119
01:23:21,396 --> 01:23:22,646
For the first time in…

1120
01:23:24,188 --> 01:23:25,105
eight years.

1121
01:23:25,938 --> 01:23:27,605
It was me who protected her from Appa.

1122
01:23:32,521 --> 01:23:33,896
Is this the havoc you spoke of?

1123
01:23:36,021 --> 01:23:37,021
That's not even the half of it.

1124
01:23:39,230 --> 01:23:40,438
Here's the worst part.

1125
01:23:40,730 --> 01:23:43,980
He got black magic
performed at Kusuma's grave.

1126
01:23:49,063 --> 01:23:51,688
- Is this another story or…
- This isn't a story, sir.

1127
01:23:51,980 --> 01:23:54,480
It's the truth.
I'm telling you like I saw it.

1128
01:24:15,021 --> 01:24:16,355
Get back to work. Go.

1129
01:24:17,646 --> 01:24:18,521
He won't believe me.

1130
01:24:19,313 --> 01:24:20,605
He never believed me.

1131
01:24:20,980 --> 01:24:22,396
Let him go in.

1132
01:24:22,688 --> 01:24:24,146
Appa will scare the daylights out of him,

1133
01:24:24,396 --> 01:24:25,313
and then he'll believe me.

1134
01:24:29,271 --> 01:24:32,521
No, no, no.
What you said is not right, Gandhi.

1135
01:24:33,396 --> 01:24:34,355
Why only poor men?

1136
01:24:35,563 --> 01:24:38,480
They're not the only ones
contributing to overpopulation.

1137
01:24:39,021 --> 01:24:41,105
You think we rich men are any better?

1138
01:24:41,813 --> 01:24:43,646
We sowed our seeds everywhere, didn't we?

1139
01:24:45,021 --> 01:24:46,355
What does a poor man know anyway?

1140
01:24:46,813 --> 01:24:48,313
He's just a soldier waiting to die.

1141
01:24:49,271 --> 01:24:52,105
It was kings who stole kingdoms
and screwed queens.

1142
01:24:52,813 --> 01:24:53,730
And yet,

1143
01:24:53,938 --> 01:24:57,563
you tortured and castrated the poor
to curb the population.

1144
01:24:58,021 --> 01:24:59,355
Did it change anything, Mr ?

1145
01:25:01,063 --> 01:25:04,313
The population grew so much
no son could tell who his father was.

1146
01:25:05,480 --> 01:25:06,355
Anyway, Mr.

1147
01:25:07,063 --> 01:25:09,146
can a mistake be rectified
by killing the culprit?

1148
01:25:09,438 --> 01:25:11,230
We need to find the
root cause of the problem.

1149
01:25:11,855 --> 01:25:12,896
And what is that, tell me?

1150
01:25:13,605 --> 01:25:14,563
Oh my!

1151
01:25:15,146 --> 01:25:17,688
How did you become a leader
with no basic awareness?

1152
01:25:18,146 --> 01:25:20,605
Lack of awareness is
the root cause of the problem.

1153
01:25:21,230 --> 01:25:23,145
You must spread awareness if you can.

1154
01:25:23,146 --> 01:25:25,396
You can't just go
around sterilizing people.

1155
01:25:27,396 --> 01:25:29,980
Why are you making me spell this out?

1156
01:25:32,521 --> 01:25:33,396
Achari?

1157
01:25:35,521 --> 01:25:36,688
When did you come?

1158
01:25:37,813 --> 01:25:38,980
It's been a while.

1159
01:25:39,396 --> 01:25:41,730
You were in an important meeting, so…

1160
01:25:41,896 --> 01:25:43,313
To hell with your modesty.

1161
01:25:43,521 --> 01:25:44,688
Come, I'll introduce you.

1162
01:25:45,355 --> 01:25:46,230
Mr.

1163
01:25:46,896 --> 01:25:48,771
He's my friend, Dr. Achari.

1164
01:25:51,896 --> 01:25:53,063
Say hi to this great man.

1165
01:25:56,063 --> 01:25:58,896
- Is he Mr. ?
- Yes. Our very own Mr.

1166
01:25:59,771 --> 01:26:01,980
Namaste, sir.

1167
01:26:02,105 --> 01:26:05,855
Never thought I'd meet the man
who brought us freedom.

1168
01:26:06,938 --> 01:26:07,980
Freedom?

1169
01:26:09,063 --> 01:26:10,105
What freedom?

1170
01:26:10,938 --> 01:26:14,396
I mean, he brought us independence, no?

1171
01:26:14,730 --> 01:26:17,813
Oh, silly! He's not the one
who brought us freedom.

1172
01:26:17,938 --> 01:26:19,563
He's that person who took away
the poor man's freedom.

1173
01:26:20,896 --> 01:26:21,771
Oh!

1174
01:26:22,230 --> 01:26:23,605
So, he's San--

1175
01:26:26,021 --> 01:26:29,063
The person you said brought us freedom.
But not freedom of speech.

1176
01:26:29,563 --> 01:26:30,896
Don't say it out loud.
Someone could hear you.

1177
01:26:31,896 --> 01:26:34,730
Yes, you're right! It's him.
Didn't you recognize him?

1178
01:26:34,938 --> 01:26:37,730
I would've, if I could see him.

1179
01:26:39,480 --> 01:26:40,480
You can't see him?

1180
01:26:40,855 --> 01:26:43,605
It's been 10 years since
he died in our world.

1181
01:26:45,980 --> 01:26:46,938
He died?

1182
01:26:47,938 --> 01:26:48,855
How?

1183
01:26:50,521 --> 01:26:51,980
Well.

1184
01:26:52,521 --> 01:26:56,105
Some say he flew a plane
wearing Kolhapuri sandals.

1185
01:26:57,230 --> 01:26:59,813
Some say other things.

1186
01:27:00,146 --> 01:27:04,563
But the world believes
it was a plane crash.

1187
01:27:04,896 --> 01:27:07,980
Why don't you ask him yourself?

1188
01:27:09,480 --> 01:27:10,437
Ask whom?

1189
01:27:10,438 --> 01:27:13,105
Uh, Mr. Fill-in-the-blank Gandhi.

1190
01:27:17,521 --> 01:27:18,480
How can I ask him?

1191
01:27:19,688 --> 01:27:20,896
You said he's dead.

1192
01:27:21,938 --> 01:27:23,270
And it is personal to me.

1193
01:27:23,271 --> 01:27:25,396
Can't just ask anyone. Take this.

1194
01:27:26,480 --> 01:27:27,437
What for?

1195
01:27:27,438 --> 01:27:28,938
"Liquid Courage", as you call it.

1196
01:27:29,063 --> 01:27:31,313
- Yeah, but why now?
- Just drink it.

1197
01:27:33,105 --> 01:27:34,855
Chug, chug, chug!

1198
01:27:36,105 --> 01:27:37,563
Why do I need courage now?

1199
01:27:39,480 --> 01:27:40,396
Well…

1200
01:27:42,146 --> 01:27:43,980
To know the truth, of course!

1201
01:27:44,188 --> 01:27:46,354
You said we could run the tests…

1202
01:27:46,355 --> 01:27:47,896
if we had something from his body, right?

1203
01:27:51,355 --> 01:27:52,855
There are some things there.
Go take them.

1204
01:28:17,938 --> 01:28:18,896
Ramudu!

1205
01:28:19,855 --> 01:28:20,896
What have you done, man?

1206
01:28:29,355 --> 01:28:32,313
I know I didn't invite you to
the ceremony we had last week.

1207
01:28:33,813 --> 01:28:34,855
Sorry, man.

1208
01:28:36,521 --> 01:28:37,771
Please don't mind.

1209
01:29:24,146 --> 01:29:25,271
Dad?

1210
01:29:26,813 --> 01:29:27,730
Dad?

1211
01:29:28,813 --> 01:29:29,688
Dad!

1212
01:29:44,313 --> 01:29:45,188
Who are you?

1213
01:29:45,938 --> 01:29:48,145
It's me, Dad. Kusuma.

1214
01:29:48,146 --> 01:29:49,605
Kusuma?

1215
01:29:50,855 --> 01:29:53,688
- Didn't you die?
- I died in my world, Dad.

1216
01:29:53,855 --> 01:29:57,646
But you're not letting
me leave your world.

1217
01:29:57,855 --> 01:30:00,271
Go, son. Go, go.

1218
01:30:07,771 --> 01:30:08,770
Don't come close!

1219
01:30:08,771 --> 01:30:10,812
- Don't touch me!
- Dad, wait!

1220
01:30:10,813 --> 01:30:11,938
Dad, wait!

1221
01:30:12,063 --> 01:30:13,855
Wait, Dad!

1222
01:30:17,063 --> 01:30:18,646
Dad, stop!

1223
01:30:21,855 --> 01:30:23,230
Dad, stop!

1224
01:30:43,063 --> 01:30:45,354
- Don't touch me!
- Fine.

1225
01:30:45,355 --> 01:30:47,230
I won't touch you. Don't be scared, dad.

1226
01:30:47,480 --> 01:30:48,396
You think I'm scared?

1227
01:30:50,021 --> 01:30:51,437
Why are you even here?

1228
01:30:51,438 --> 01:30:53,813
I'm here to help you, dad.

1229
01:30:54,063 --> 01:30:55,312
You're not even the size
of my little finger.

1230
01:30:55,313 --> 01:30:56,562
How can you help me?

1231
01:30:56,563 --> 01:30:58,313
I might not be as big as your finger.

1232
01:30:58,438 --> 01:31:01,896
I know my little finger's nail is
as good as gold to you.

1233
01:31:02,105 --> 01:31:03,896
I couldn't bear to see your struggle.

1234
01:31:04,021 --> 01:31:06,688
- So, I'm here to help.
- Really?

1235
01:31:07,021 --> 01:31:11,688
You need something
from my body, don't you?

1236
01:31:11,813 --> 01:31:15,937
Yes, I searched your whole
room and found nothing.

1237
01:31:15,938 --> 01:31:19,520
I know exactly how to
get you what you need.

1238
01:31:19,521 --> 01:31:20,438
Is it?

1239
01:31:21,105 --> 01:31:22,230
Kiddo! Kiddo!

1240
01:31:22,813 --> 01:31:24,688
Please show me some grace and tell me.

1241
01:31:24,938 --> 01:31:26,104
I'll be reborn as your son.

1242
01:31:26,105 --> 01:31:29,730
No, no. Lord knows who your father is.

1243
01:31:31,105 --> 01:31:34,896
Tell me, and I'll build you a
tomb with Makrana marble.

1244
01:31:35,188 --> 01:31:37,020
Deal. Come along.

1245
01:31:37,021 --> 01:31:38,229
I said, don't touch me!

1246
01:31:38,230 --> 01:31:39,813
I thought you wanted my help.

1247
01:31:52,396 --> 01:31:54,605
Will you really build me a marble tomb?

1248
01:31:56,813 --> 01:32:00,688
- Once I give my word--
- Yeah, yeah. Got it. Let's go.

1249
01:32:16,105 --> 01:32:18,771
Why did you bring me here?

1250
01:32:19,480 --> 01:32:20,355
I'll tell you.

1251
01:32:20,771 --> 01:32:22,230
First, answer my question.

1252
01:32:24,813 --> 01:32:26,271
Who is that?

1253
01:32:32,230 --> 01:32:34,855
That's my great-great-great-grandfather.

1254
01:32:35,813 --> 01:32:37,270
The founding father of my dynasty.

1255
01:32:37,271 --> 01:32:38,605
And, how is this guy related to me?

1256
01:32:40,688 --> 01:32:43,438
What do you mean by "this guy"?

1257
01:32:43,896 --> 01:32:46,520
His Highness…
is in no way related to you.

1258
01:32:46,521 --> 01:32:49,271
He's my great-great-great-grandfather.

1259
01:32:50,063 --> 01:32:51,021
Then, who's that?

1260
01:32:52,771 --> 01:32:53,812
He's my grandfather.

1261
01:32:53,813 --> 01:32:57,312
How is this guy…
I mean, His Highness, related to me?

1262
01:32:57,313 --> 01:32:58,604
What is His Highness to me?

1263
01:32:58,605 --> 01:33:01,355
Nothing! He's my grandfather.

1264
01:33:04,146 --> 01:33:05,771
So, he's not related to me either?

1265
01:33:07,438 --> 01:33:08,896
Then, who's that?

1266
01:33:11,146 --> 01:33:12,562
He's my father.

1267
01:33:12,563 --> 01:33:14,605
- How--
- He's nothing to you. Stop asking.

1268
01:33:14,855 --> 01:33:16,980
Fine, I won't ask. Chill.

1269
01:33:18,271 --> 01:33:19,938
Now, who is she?

1270
01:33:24,521 --> 01:33:25,855
She's my mother.

1271
01:33:26,938 --> 01:33:30,146
She died giving birth to me.

1272
01:33:34,521 --> 01:33:36,313
Calm down, Dad. Calm down.

1273
01:33:36,771 --> 01:33:40,271
I know how it feels
to lose your loved ones.

1274
01:33:40,438 --> 01:33:42,145
Don't cry. Calm down.

1275
01:33:42,146 --> 01:33:43,313
And who's this guy?

1276
01:33:45,563 --> 01:33:46,438
Up here!

1277
01:33:48,646 --> 01:33:50,730
That's the question that haunts me.

1278
01:33:51,146 --> 01:33:52,770
You offered to help, right?

1279
01:33:52,771 --> 01:33:56,812
Why are you grilling me like this?

1280
01:33:56,813 --> 01:34:00,063
What's the rush?
Come close. I'll tell you something.

1281
01:34:01,896 --> 01:34:04,188
- What is it?
- You were right.

1282
01:34:04,355 --> 01:34:06,021
None of them are related to me.

1283
01:34:06,230 --> 01:34:08,271
Isn't this what you wanted to know?

1284
01:34:08,521 --> 01:34:10,063
Now make peace with me and come.

1285
01:34:10,230 --> 01:34:11,938
We can both hang on the wall.

1286
01:34:12,105 --> 01:34:14,520
Oh sure! You're some big official.

1287
01:34:14,521 --> 01:34:16,437
The President has
approved your statement.

1288
01:34:16,438 --> 01:34:18,605
And I'm supposed to believe
you like a thumb-sucking child?

1289
01:34:19,271 --> 01:34:22,063
Quit the bullshit and tell
me where to find your things.

1290
01:34:22,188 --> 01:34:24,980
- One last question
- No! No more questions.

1291
01:34:25,271 --> 01:34:29,355
- Tell me or I'll figure it out myself.
- Dad, wait, wait.

1292
01:34:29,688 --> 01:34:31,813
If you answer this question,

1293
01:34:31,938 --> 01:34:33,771
it's a straight road to my things.

1294
01:34:34,813 --> 01:34:35,938
One last question.

1295
01:34:36,605 --> 01:34:40,688
What is it that everyone
on this wall has that I don't?

1296
01:34:45,188 --> 01:34:47,188
- Our royal blood.
- Nonsense.

1297
01:34:47,688 --> 01:34:48,854
You'll never change.

1298
01:34:48,855 --> 01:34:51,270
Fine, as long as I'm here,

1299
01:34:51,271 --> 01:34:53,437
the mystery will keep bugging you.

1300
01:34:53,438 --> 01:34:56,396
I'm leaving. You think of the answer.

1301
01:34:56,646 --> 01:34:59,312
If you get the answer,
you'll find what you want.

1302
01:34:59,313 --> 01:35:00,188
Hey, wait!

1303
01:35:00,438 --> 01:35:02,646
Kusuma! Tell the answer and go. Hey!

1304
01:35:03,146 --> 01:35:05,021
You're from such a great dynasty.

1305
01:35:05,188 --> 01:35:07,395
If such a low-born reveals the answer,

1306
01:35:07,396 --> 01:35:08,980
isn't it shameful to your dynasty?

1307
01:35:11,105 --> 01:35:12,105
That's true.

1308
01:35:13,605 --> 01:35:14,688
I'll find the answer.

1309
01:35:15,646 --> 01:35:17,646
- You go.
- Fine. Bye, dad.

1310
01:35:18,063 --> 01:35:20,771
I'll smack you if you call me that again.

1311
01:35:48,313 --> 01:35:49,855
Sir! Lavana sir!

1312
01:35:50,021 --> 01:35:51,105
Your father is crying.

1313
01:36:06,313 --> 01:36:07,230
Dad?

1314
01:36:10,771 --> 01:36:11,730
Dad?

1315
01:36:14,980 --> 01:36:16,896
Lavana, you're here!

1316
01:36:19,813 --> 01:36:20,938
What happened, dad?

1317
01:36:21,813 --> 01:36:22,980
Why are you crying?

1318
01:36:25,230 --> 01:36:26,355
Don't cry, dad.

1319
01:36:27,063 --> 01:36:28,896
Oh, Lavana!

1320
01:36:29,146 --> 01:36:33,605
Last night, Kusuma showed up in my dream.

1321
01:36:37,938 --> 01:36:38,938
Achchamma, where are you going?

1322
01:36:39,896 --> 01:36:42,271
I wondered why he was crying.

1323
01:36:43,271 --> 01:36:44,730
It's just about Kusuma.

1324
01:36:44,980 --> 01:36:46,730
I'll get back to my work.

1325
01:36:47,105 --> 01:36:48,146
You deal with him.

1326
01:36:49,230 --> 01:36:50,230
Hey, Achchamma!

1327
01:36:52,521 --> 01:36:53,896
Don't cry, Dad.

1328
01:36:55,438 --> 01:36:57,104
- Don't cry, Dad.
- Lavana…

1329
01:36:57,105 --> 01:36:58,479
Fine, how is Kusuma?

1330
01:36:58,480 --> 01:37:00,479
He's crying too.

1331
01:37:00,480 --> 01:37:02,896
Why? What's bothering him?

1332
01:37:05,063 --> 01:37:06,646
The royal turban.

1333
01:37:06,896 --> 01:37:07,855
Turban?

1334
01:37:08,855 --> 01:37:10,729
- What do you mean?
- Hey, Lavana.

1335
01:37:10,730 --> 01:37:13,396
What do we do when
someone in our dynasty dies?

1336
01:37:13,521 --> 01:37:14,813
When someone dies?

1337
01:37:15,563 --> 01:37:17,230
If married, we cremate them.

1338
01:37:17,521 --> 01:37:18,729
If not, we bury them.

1339
01:37:18,730 --> 01:37:21,395
Not that! Don't we
adorn the dead with a turban

1340
01:37:21,396 --> 01:37:24,271
and send them off in a royal procession?

1341
01:37:24,646 --> 01:37:25,855
Yeah, so?

1342
01:37:25,980 --> 01:37:28,854
That's why your little
brother is distressed.

1343
01:37:28,855 --> 01:37:32,145
He said, "The whole town gossiped
as I had no procession."

1344
01:37:32,146 --> 01:37:34,854
"You sent me off without
a royal turban."

1345
01:37:34,855 --> 01:37:38,105
My poor child cried all night.

1346
01:37:40,605 --> 01:37:43,938
We must place the turban on him.
Make the arrangements.

1347
01:37:44,396 --> 01:37:45,896
What are you saying, Dad?

1348
01:37:46,230 --> 01:37:47,730
He died eight years ago.

1349
01:37:47,896 --> 01:37:49,354
How can we honor him now?

1350
01:37:49,355 --> 01:37:52,020
What if he's dead?
He's still in our backyard.

1351
01:37:52,021 --> 01:37:53,271
Have the workers dig up his grave.

1352
01:37:53,521 --> 01:37:56,438
Stop it. Your madness has gone too far.

1353
01:37:56,646 --> 01:37:57,771
Do you hear yourself?

1354
01:37:57,896 --> 01:38:00,105
He's your little brother, Lavana.

1355
01:38:00,313 --> 01:38:02,813
Isn't it your duty to
fulfill his last wish?

1356
01:38:02,938 --> 01:38:05,855
Yes! I would've done whatever
he wanted if he were alive.

1357
01:38:06,021 --> 01:38:08,355
But I can't indulge your
delusions and do as you say.

1358
01:38:08,688 --> 01:38:10,562
- Stop dreaming such nonsense.
- La…

1359
01:38:10,563 --> 01:38:12,063
- Have a drink and go to sleep.
- Lavana! Wait.

1360
01:38:35,813 --> 01:38:37,188
I knew it.

1361
01:38:38,063 --> 01:38:39,688
You always envied him.

1362
01:38:40,480 --> 01:38:43,896
That's why you always lashed out at him.

1363
01:38:44,855 --> 01:38:46,230
My poor child.

1364
01:38:46,730 --> 01:38:48,980
He must have gone through hell.

1365
01:38:49,605 --> 01:38:51,980
He died when your abuse
became unbearable for him.

1366
01:38:53,480 --> 01:38:56,480
And now, you refuse
to fulfill his last wish.

1367
01:38:58,563 --> 01:38:59,605
You're the reason.

1368
01:39:00,313 --> 01:39:02,188
You're the reason my son is dead.

1369
01:39:03,396 --> 01:39:04,563
You think I can't do this without you?

1370
01:39:05,105 --> 01:39:07,230
Open the door.

1371
01:39:08,146 --> 01:39:09,188
So, what if you refuse?

1372
01:39:09,771 --> 01:39:10,813
I'll dig my son's grave

1373
01:39:11,230 --> 01:39:15,313
and grant his last wish
with a beautiful turban.

1374
01:39:16,188 --> 01:39:17,271
Open the door!

1375
01:39:17,938 --> 01:39:19,063
Open the door!

1376
01:39:19,605 --> 01:39:20,855
Open the damn door, Lavana!

1377
01:39:21,521 --> 01:39:23,938
Open the door!

1378
01:40:09,438 --> 01:40:10,355
The job is done.

1379
01:40:12,980 --> 01:40:13,937
The job is done.

1380
01:40:13,938 --> 01:40:16,438
Just ask “Who's there?"

1381
01:40:16,605 --> 01:40:21,979
Won't the 5 senses answer to you?

1382
01:40:21,980 --> 01:40:24,355
At the sound of my name,

1383
01:40:24,605 --> 01:40:29,895
won't the waves bow down?

1384
01:40:29,896 --> 01:40:35,021
Our glow is

1385
01:40:35,271 --> 01:40:39,730
ancestral.

1386
01:40:40,688 --> 01:40:45,771
Time won't change

1387
01:40:46,021 --> 01:40:50,896
our origins.

1388
01:40:52,646 --> 01:40:57,646
Our tale is eternal.

1389
01:40:57,938 --> 01:41:01,271
There is no mistake or mishap

1390
01:41:07,271 --> 01:41:09,188
that you can escape.

1391
01:41:12,605 --> 01:41:14,438
I will reveal your secrets.

1392
01:41:17,938 --> 01:41:19,771
I will pull your strings.

1393
01:41:23,271 --> 01:41:25,104
I will ruffle up the bushes.

1394
01:41:25,105 --> 01:41:27,021
All 4 directions will bow down.

1395
01:41:27,230 --> 01:41:29,771
The land will flourish as you walk.

1396
01:41:29,938 --> 01:41:32,271
If you raise your eyebrows,

1397
01:41:32,688 --> 01:41:35,188
the trembling
universe will be visible.

1398
01:41:59,230 --> 01:42:02,020
You are me, I am you.

1399
01:42:02,021 --> 01:42:03,855
Right, daddy dearest?

1400
01:42:04,605 --> 01:42:09,105
It's you in my walk and talk.

1401
01:42:15,313 --> 01:42:16,479
My eyes and nose,

1402
01:42:16,480 --> 01:42:19,813
all of it resembles
you, daddy dearest.

1403
01:42:20,563 --> 01:42:21,812
If you look at me with love,

1404
01:42:21,813 --> 01:42:25,146
you can see yourself in me.

1405
01:42:25,938 --> 01:42:28,313
Look at me closely,

1406
01:42:28,605 --> 01:42:33,396
every inch resembles
you, daddy dearest.

1407
01:42:33,938 --> 01:42:36,604
Can you tell milk and water apart?

1408
01:42:36,605 --> 01:42:39,105
Why relate this swan to a crow?

1409
01:42:39,271 --> 01:42:41,979
How are you related to this tree?

1410
01:42:41,980 --> 01:42:44,687
It isn't enough to be
a sapling under its shade.

1411
01:42:44,688 --> 01:42:48,980
A weed in the garden.

1412
01:42:49,938 --> 01:42:54,271
There's something
wrong with your math.

1413
01:42:55,313 --> 01:42:57,979
I will detangle all the
knots in your head.

1414
01:42:57,980 --> 01:43:00,687
I will reveal which plant
this seed belongs to.

1415
01:43:00,688 --> 01:43:03,312
I will squeeze the
sap out of the roots.

1416
01:43:03,313 --> 01:43:05,938
I will bring evidence of the truth.

1417
01:43:09,980 --> 01:43:11,771
You cannot escape.

1418
01:43:15,105 --> 01:43:16,980
I will reveal your secrets.

1419
01:43:20,438 --> 01:43:22,480
I will pull your strings.

1420
01:43:25,730 --> 01:43:27,270
I will ruffle up the bushes.

1421
01:43:27,271 --> 01:43:29,688
All 4 directions will bow down.

1422
01:43:29,938 --> 01:43:32,396
The land will flourish as you walk.

1423
01:43:32,605 --> 01:43:35,063
If you raise your eyebrows,

1424
01:43:35,313 --> 01:43:37,771
the trembling
universe will be visible.

1425
01:43:56,855 --> 01:43:58,563
What is this madness, sir?

1426
01:43:59,855 --> 01:44:00,938
It's my karma.

1427
01:44:22,938 --> 01:44:25,563
My child!

1428
01:44:27,855 --> 01:44:28,896
Oh my!

1429
01:44:32,355 --> 01:44:34,521
Look at what you've become.

1430
01:44:34,646 --> 01:44:37,770
He used to shine like a black berry.

1431
01:44:37,771 --> 01:44:41,730
Look at him now, so white and pale.

1432
01:44:45,438 --> 01:44:46,563
Pass that, please.

1433
01:44:53,730 --> 01:44:54,813
My child.

1434
01:44:55,188 --> 01:44:56,063
My child.

1435
01:45:32,813 --> 01:45:34,188
You little rascal!

1436
01:45:35,063 --> 01:45:36,771
You crawl to my room
from down here, isn't it?

1437
01:45:41,438 --> 01:45:43,563
Wait! You'll pay for this!

1438
01:45:47,771 --> 01:45:48,813
My son!

1439
01:45:58,146 --> 01:45:59,605
Sir, you called for me?

1440
01:46:01,271 --> 01:46:03,229
You tried to steal these pumpkins, right?

1441
01:46:03,230 --> 01:46:04,187
But sir…

1442
01:46:04,188 --> 01:46:06,105
I put them back when my
mother-in-law reprimanded me.

1443
01:46:06,230 --> 01:46:07,313
Do you want them now?

1444
01:46:08,771 --> 01:46:09,855
Take him away!

1445
01:46:33,230 --> 01:46:35,813
Not one or two,
I brought you three things.

1446
01:46:36,438 --> 01:46:37,355
These will do, right?

1447
01:46:39,480 --> 01:46:40,521
What are you waiting for?

1448
01:46:40,938 --> 01:46:42,438
Take them and begin the tests.

1449
01:46:46,396 --> 01:46:47,271
Ramudu!

1450
01:46:48,563 --> 01:46:49,480
What's this?

1451
01:46:50,521 --> 01:46:52,813
I said it casually.
But you've gone too far. It's unjust.

1452
01:46:52,938 --> 01:46:53,855
Unjust?

1453
01:46:54,271 --> 01:46:56,396
Injustice and immorality
are not in my blood.

1454
01:46:56,771 --> 01:46:58,771
You think he just gave them to me?
Come, I'll show you.

1455
01:47:04,271 --> 01:47:06,230
There, look!

1456
01:47:09,563 --> 01:47:10,480
Look!

1457
01:47:10,813 --> 01:47:12,230
Shah Jahan's wife's tomb,

1458
01:47:12,355 --> 01:47:15,813
the Taj Mahal, built with
the same Makrana marble.

1459
01:47:16,480 --> 01:47:17,355
{\an8}Look!

1460
01:47:17,605 --> 01:47:19,271
Not even his own father
would've done this for him.

1461
01:47:25,730 --> 01:47:26,771
Don't you believe me?

1462
01:47:27,813 --> 01:47:30,355
Many great monuments are
made of Makrana marble.

1463
01:47:31,480 --> 01:47:32,938
The Moti Masjid in Pakistan.

1464
01:47:33,480 --> 01:47:36,646
The Victoria Memorial we
visited in Brahmanda Nagaram.

1465
01:47:36,771 --> 01:47:38,355
That's Makrana marble too.

1466
01:47:39,063 --> 01:47:40,812
And recently, in Dubai--

1467
01:47:40,813 --> 01:47:42,146
Shut up, you lunatic!

1468
01:47:46,521 --> 01:47:48,354
You go from one obsession to another!

1469
01:47:48,355 --> 01:47:50,646
Why are you like this, man?

1470
01:48:12,271 --> 01:48:13,146
Ramudu.

1471
01:48:14,396 --> 01:48:15,438
Achari.

1472
01:48:17,438 --> 01:48:19,980
Can liver cancer cause jaw pain?

1473
01:48:21,688 --> 01:48:23,188
How are liver and jaw related?

1474
01:48:25,230 --> 01:48:27,438
- There's no such thing.
- Right?

1475
01:48:28,771 --> 01:48:31,480
I have a sudden pain in my jaw.

1476
01:48:32,480 --> 01:48:34,730
I was worried it was
due to my liver cancer.

1477
01:48:38,605 --> 01:48:40,896
Anyway, take those and get the test done.

1478
01:48:42,146 --> 01:48:43,188
Do you even hear yourself?

1479
01:48:43,563 --> 01:48:45,020
Do you think this is black magic?

1480
01:48:45,021 --> 01:48:48,396
You hand over some bones and
find out if he's your son?

1481
01:48:51,188 --> 01:48:53,230
Since you asked, I
looked into the process.

1482
01:48:53,480 --> 01:48:55,313
DNA testing is no child's play.

1483
01:48:55,438 --> 01:48:57,980
The police and lawyers must be involved.

1484
01:48:58,438 --> 01:48:59,729
Unless there's a crime,

1485
01:48:59,730 --> 01:49:02,438
the court won't let the
police run such tests.

1486
01:49:02,938 --> 01:49:05,188
So, listen to me and let this go.

1487
01:49:25,855 --> 01:49:27,855
Now I see

1488
01:49:29,605 --> 01:49:33,021
why you slapped me for
digging up the grave.

1489
01:49:34,896 --> 01:49:39,646
I suspected many people.

1490
01:49:41,230 --> 01:49:44,396
But I never thought you,

1491
01:49:45,605 --> 01:49:48,938
my childhood best friend,
would stab me in the back.

1492
01:49:50,230 --> 01:49:51,313
Hey, Ramudu!

1493
01:49:52,855 --> 01:49:54,105
What are you saying?

1494
01:49:55,771 --> 01:49:57,146
I can understand.

1495
01:49:59,188 --> 01:50:00,896
Digging up his son's
grave without asking

1496
01:50:01,313 --> 01:50:02,563
would anger any father.

1497
01:50:02,896 --> 01:50:04,230
Your anger is justified.

1498
01:50:04,563 --> 01:50:05,980
Hey, this is unfair, man.

1499
01:50:07,146 --> 01:50:08,105
Don't say that.

1500
01:50:09,480 --> 01:50:12,271
It's my fault. It's all my fault.

1501
01:50:12,771 --> 01:50:14,480
Trusting you was my biggest fault.

1502
01:50:15,313 --> 01:50:16,646
But, but,

1503
01:50:17,188 --> 01:50:18,771
but, but…

1504
01:50:20,730 --> 01:50:21,605
How…

1505
01:50:37,813 --> 01:50:41,021
Hit me! Go ahead and hit me!

1506
01:50:44,188 --> 01:50:47,104
You're afraid I'll know
the truth if we run the test.

1507
01:50:47,105 --> 01:50:48,938
That's why you refuse to do it, right?

1508
01:51:01,771 --> 01:51:02,646
Not enough.

1509
01:51:03,980 --> 01:51:04,855
Not enough.

1510
01:51:08,271 --> 01:51:09,396
I know!

1511
01:51:12,313 --> 01:51:13,355
If we run the test,

1512
01:51:13,813 --> 01:51:16,271
the doubt around his
birth will be cleared.

1513
01:51:16,396 --> 01:51:21,146
And it will prove that your
blood runs in his veins.

1514
01:51:24,521 --> 01:51:25,521
Still not enough.

1515
01:51:28,313 --> 01:51:29,896
I know you're still here.

1516
01:51:30,938 --> 01:51:32,355
Why did you run off?

1517
01:51:34,355 --> 01:51:35,480
That's why they say

1518
01:51:36,438 --> 01:51:38,355
the truth is a hard pill to swallow.

1519
01:51:40,855 --> 01:51:42,480
If I'm really deluded,

1520
01:51:43,271 --> 01:51:45,021
show me the truth.

1521
01:51:50,021 --> 01:51:51,813
If what I believe is false,

1522
01:51:52,105 --> 01:51:54,771
show me the truth.

1523
01:51:55,355 --> 01:51:56,396
Show me!

1524
01:52:03,980 --> 01:52:04,855
Ramudu!

1525
01:52:05,105 --> 01:52:06,230
- Stay away from my father!
- Hey…

1526
01:52:08,855 --> 01:52:11,479
- Don't touch him.
- I need to check on him.

1527
01:52:11,480 --> 01:52:12,605
I know what happened.

1528
01:52:14,021 --> 01:52:15,021
I know everything.

1529
01:52:22,980 --> 01:52:23,855
Dad?

1530
01:52:25,313 --> 01:52:26,271
Dad?

1531
01:52:27,813 --> 01:52:28,688
Dad?

1532
01:52:32,813 --> 01:52:34,688
<i>His organs are failing one by one.</i>

1533
01:52:35,021 --> 01:52:36,438
His heart is barely moving.

1534
01:52:37,646 --> 01:52:38,605
Probably two days.

1535
01:52:43,105 --> 01:52:44,730
<i>Take him home and</i>

1536
01:52:44,896 --> 01:52:46,563
<i>let him sleep in his royal attire.</i>

1537
01:52:47,188 --> 01:52:49,230
<i>Call all your relatives.</i>

1538
01:52:50,605 --> 01:52:53,063
<i>Let him die a king's
death in his own court.</i>

1539
01:52:53,355 --> 01:52:54,438
<i>Why in this battlefield?</i>

1540
01:53:20,063 --> 01:53:20,938
What happened?

1541
01:53:23,896 --> 01:53:25,021
Nothing yet.

1542
01:53:27,355 --> 01:53:29,355
I'll take care of him. You can go.

1543
01:53:33,480 --> 01:53:37,980
BHUVANA'S ESTATE

1544
01:54:10,855 --> 01:54:12,146
Who are you looking for, sir?

1545
01:54:13,480 --> 01:54:15,271
Bhuvanam Ramappa Rao Bahadur.

1546
01:54:16,730 --> 01:54:17,605
Is he here?

1547
01:54:20,063 --> 01:54:21,563
Let me call his son.

1548
01:54:27,355 --> 01:54:28,230
What's this?

1549
01:54:31,021 --> 01:54:31,979
This?

1550
01:54:31,980 --> 01:54:35,938
Ramappa sir's father killed
a huge crocodile with a single bullet.

1551
01:54:36,105 --> 01:54:38,021
This is its head.
We kept it as a souvenir.

1552
01:54:39,896 --> 01:54:43,938
So, the people here have
a habit of killing, huh?

1553
01:54:44,730 --> 01:54:47,938
Is Mr. Ramappa into killing too?

1554
01:54:48,146 --> 01:54:50,229
Initially, not at all.

1555
01:54:50,230 --> 01:54:52,105
It all started after his father died.

1556
01:54:53,980 --> 01:54:54,896
I have a doubt.

1557
01:54:57,355 --> 01:55:00,855
If this crocodile had killed your master,

1558
01:55:01,188 --> 01:55:02,855
would you display his head here?

1559
01:55:04,438 --> 01:55:05,313
As a souvenir?

1560
01:55:40,105 --> 01:55:41,313
Wait here, sir.

1561
01:55:41,521 --> 01:55:43,021
I'll go get his son.

1562
01:56:02,855 --> 01:56:04,188
- This is?
- His son.

1563
01:56:04,646 --> 01:56:05,980
I am Mr. Ramappa's son.

1564
01:56:06,480 --> 01:56:07,563
- The elder son?
- Yes.

1565
01:56:08,480 --> 01:56:09,355
Nice meeting you.

1566
01:56:25,980 --> 01:56:27,313
You have a younger brother, don't you?

1567
01:56:28,355 --> 01:56:29,230
Had.

1568
01:56:30,438 --> 01:56:31,480
Come here, ma'am.

1569
01:56:32,063 --> 01:56:34,104
- What's your name?
- Achchamma, sir.

1570
01:56:34,105 --> 01:56:36,188
Achchamma, just go back down.

1571
01:56:36,396 --> 01:56:38,229
There's a man in the jeep I came in.

1572
01:56:38,230 --> 01:56:39,105
Bring him here.

1573
01:56:41,313 --> 01:56:42,480
Will he be alone, sir?

1574
01:56:43,271 --> 01:56:45,980
- I can't recognize him, right?
- Good question.

1575
01:56:46,396 --> 01:56:49,813
He's a very dark-skinned
man in his forties.

1576
01:56:50,230 --> 01:56:52,938
- Look for that. You'll find him.
- Okay.

1577
01:56:54,146 --> 01:56:55,313
What happened, Lavana?

1578
01:56:56,188 --> 01:56:58,230
He wants to talk to my father.

1579
01:56:59,021 --> 01:57:01,271
- But you interfered.
- Talk to your father?

1580
01:57:03,230 --> 01:57:04,187
What happened, sir?

1581
01:57:04,188 --> 01:57:06,521
Sorry. May I ask who you are?

1582
01:57:06,771 --> 01:57:08,063
I am Dr. Narayanachari.

1583
01:57:08,855 --> 01:57:10,979
Ramappa's close friend and well-wisher.

1584
01:57:10,980 --> 01:57:12,146
Okay, please sit.

1585
01:57:14,896 --> 01:57:15,771
So…

1586
01:57:16,396 --> 01:57:18,812
I need to interrogate Mr. Ramappa once.

1587
01:57:18,813 --> 01:57:19,813
- Interrogate?
- Interrogate?

1588
01:57:23,980 --> 01:57:24,980
About what, Inspector?

1589
01:57:25,730 --> 01:57:26,646
I'll tell you.

1590
01:57:27,521 --> 01:57:29,438
Ramappa sir's second son.

1591
01:57:31,105 --> 01:57:32,062
Kusumappa?

1592
01:57:32,063 --> 01:57:33,771
Yes, Kusumappa.

1593
01:57:34,355 --> 01:57:36,105
Claiming he wasn't Mr. Ramappa's son,

1594
01:57:36,605 --> 01:57:40,688
a man told me his wife sold their
two-month-old without his knowledge…

1595
01:57:41,063 --> 01:57:43,563
to Mr. Ramappa for 100 rupees.

1596
01:57:44,271 --> 01:57:48,521
And that sometime ago,
Mr. Ramappa killed that child.

1597
01:57:49,355 --> 01:57:51,521
These were that man's exact words.

1598
01:57:52,188 --> 01:57:53,063
What?

1599
01:57:53,355 --> 01:57:54,312
Yes.

1600
01:57:54,313 --> 01:57:55,480
- But my father
- Shush.

1601
01:57:58,771 --> 01:57:59,688
See, Inspector.

1602
01:58:00,480 --> 01:58:02,688
This guy seems desperate
to squeeze out money.

1603
01:58:03,396 --> 01:58:05,021
Kusuma is our Ramappa's son.

1604
01:58:05,855 --> 01:58:07,063
None of those things happened.

1605
01:58:08,146 --> 01:58:10,355
- And I am a witness to that.
- Yes, Inspector.

1606
01:58:11,605 --> 01:58:13,021
My father didn't kill Kusuma.

1607
01:58:13,480 --> 01:58:15,563
He fell into the pond
and died before my eyes.

1608
01:58:16,480 --> 01:58:17,355
Yes.

1609
01:58:17,646 --> 01:58:20,563
So, half the case you made is a lie.

1610
01:58:23,313 --> 01:58:25,688
What? Half of it is a lie?

1611
01:58:27,313 --> 01:58:28,855
Kusuma is not my father's son.

1612
01:58:29,605 --> 01:58:31,645
I've doubted it ever since
I was a child.

1613
01:58:31,646 --> 01:58:33,021
What are you saying Lavana?

1614
01:58:33,563 --> 01:58:35,355
- Have you gone mad?
- No.

1615
01:58:35,605 --> 01:58:37,355
My father went mad thanks to Kusuma.

1616
01:58:37,688 --> 01:58:40,313
- And now, he's on his deathbed.
- Shut up, Lavana.

1617
01:58:41,188 --> 01:58:43,855
Don't speak ill of the dead
without knowing the truth.

1618
01:58:43,980 --> 01:58:44,855
Doctor.

1619
01:58:45,646 --> 01:58:46,646
Let him speak.

1620
01:58:47,230 --> 01:58:49,688
I will decide what's true and what's not.

1621
01:58:50,396 --> 01:58:51,396
Please speak, Lavana.

1622
01:58:51,896 --> 01:58:55,646
Why did you suspect at such a young age

1623
01:58:56,271 --> 01:58:58,188
that your brother was
not your father's son?

1624
01:58:58,980 --> 01:59:01,855
If you saw how my father's
behavior changed after he was born,

1625
01:59:02,938 --> 01:59:03,855
anyone would…

1626
01:59:05,063 --> 01:59:06,813
feel the same.

1627
01:59:46,980 --> 01:59:49,395
Oh, grandson! How
did you turn out so dark?

1628
01:59:49,396 --> 01:59:52,605
I'm afraid my lips would
turn black if I kissed you.

1629
02:00:07,896 --> 02:00:09,896
Did I say something wrong?

1630
02:00:41,230 --> 02:00:42,187
Mom?

1631
02:00:42,188 --> 02:00:44,938
Will he turn fairer once he's scrubbed?

1632
02:00:45,105 --> 02:00:48,688
One scrub won't do it, son.
We'll give him a scrub every day.

1633
02:00:49,230 --> 02:00:54,313
<i>It's going to be alright</i>

1634
02:00:54,771 --> 02:00:57,396
<i>"Calm down, little one"</i>

1635
02:00:57,980 --> 02:01:01,438
<i>Let's wipe that darkness off your skin</i>

1636
02:01:01,980 --> 02:01:05,105
<i>Aren't you daddy's dearest, my darling?</i>

1637
02:01:05,896 --> 02:01:08,771
<i>Your dad is hurting, do you see?</i>

1638
02:01:13,271 --> 02:01:15,021
This is the second chapter of my story.

1639
02:01:19,438 --> 02:01:20,355
Hey, Ramudu.

1640
02:01:20,688 --> 02:01:21,563
Hey!

1641
02:01:23,521 --> 02:01:24,480
Hey, Ramudu!

1642
02:01:25,063 --> 02:01:25,980
Go on.

1643
02:01:26,271 --> 02:01:27,188
Thank you.

1644
02:01:28,688 --> 02:01:30,105
- What's up?
- Take a look at this.

1645
02:01:33,021 --> 02:01:36,021
The government has granted
permission for your biscuit factory.

1646
02:01:41,313 --> 02:01:43,063
Turns out Kusuma is lucky for you.

1647
02:02:09,271 --> 02:02:10,188
Dear…

1648
02:02:13,480 --> 02:02:14,938
He has turned six now.

1649
02:02:17,105 --> 02:02:19,063
Shall we send him to school?

1650
02:02:22,146 --> 02:02:24,605
Why does he need to
step out of the palace?

1651
02:02:25,896 --> 02:02:27,188
You're educated, right?

1652
02:02:28,813 --> 02:02:29,813
You homeschool him.

1653
02:02:47,105 --> 02:02:49,145
Lavana, come have your lunch.

1654
02:02:49,146 --> 02:02:51,395
Not now, Mom.
I'll have it later.

1655
02:02:51,396 --> 02:02:54,230
I'll slap you if you talk back to me!
Now move!

1656
02:03:06,313 --> 02:03:08,730
A turnover of 20 crores in six years.

1657
02:03:10,271 --> 02:03:11,771
These are the fruits of our labor.

1658
02:03:12,063 --> 02:03:13,146
On this occasion,

1659
02:03:14,146 --> 02:03:15,521
let's rebrand our company.

1660
02:03:16,105 --> 02:03:20,271
Let's put a picture of a healthy boy
on our biscuit packet.

1661
02:03:21,396 --> 02:03:22,313
What do you think?

1662
02:03:25,480 --> 02:03:27,605
Hard work can only get you so far.

1663
02:03:28,563 --> 02:03:29,730
Luck plays a major role too.

1664
02:03:30,980 --> 02:03:32,270
Ever since Kusuma was born,

1665
02:03:32,271 --> 02:03:34,271
luck hasn't left your side, Ramudu.

1666
02:03:34,896 --> 02:03:36,688
So, Kusuma's picture would be perfect.

1667
02:03:45,146 --> 02:03:46,355
Show me your strength, Lavanappa.

1668
02:03:46,896 --> 02:03:47,855
Perfect.

1669
02:03:48,188 --> 02:03:49,980
Now, flex both your arms, Lavanappa.

1670
02:03:51,730 --> 02:03:54,730
Fantastic!

1671
02:03:55,355 --> 02:03:57,021
Go get changed,
then we'll take more photos.

1672
02:04:02,396 --> 02:04:03,313
Listen.

1673
02:04:07,938 --> 02:04:10,355
Could you take a photo of him too?

1674
02:04:17,313 --> 02:04:19,230
One minute, Dad.
I'll be right back.

1675
02:04:24,771 --> 02:04:26,521
- Hey, Kusuma, what is it?
- Brother…

1676
02:04:26,730 --> 02:04:29,270
Hey! What are you doing, Kusuma?

1677
02:04:29,271 --> 02:04:31,646
Brother, let me wear this once.

1678
02:04:44,646 --> 02:04:45,521
Ready.

1679
02:04:54,938 --> 02:04:56,313
Stand properly.

1680
02:05:00,271 --> 02:05:02,480
Stand properly.

1681
02:05:09,938 --> 02:05:10,813
Hey!

1682
02:05:11,230 --> 02:05:12,396
I said stand properly!

1683
02:05:34,396 --> 02:05:35,313
Dad?

1684
02:05:37,063 --> 02:05:37,938
Lavana.

1685
02:05:40,021 --> 02:05:41,645
- How are you?
- I'm fine, Dad.

1686
02:05:41,646 --> 02:05:43,355
What did you get me from London?

1687
02:05:43,480 --> 02:05:45,854
- What's England's national sport?
- Cricket.

1688
02:05:45,855 --> 02:05:46,896
So you got a cricket kit.

1689
02:05:47,396 --> 02:05:48,271
Wow!

1690
02:05:48,396 --> 02:05:49,438
Cricket kit!

1691
02:05:51,188 --> 02:05:53,271
- Thank you, Dad!
- Get me a World Cup.

1692
02:06:10,980 --> 02:06:11,980
Dad?

1693
02:06:21,896 --> 02:06:24,605
- What?
- Did you get anything for me?

1694
02:06:27,438 --> 02:06:28,396
You're just a kid.

1695
02:06:29,355 --> 02:06:31,146
What can I get you from London?

1696
02:06:33,396 --> 02:06:35,813
Take Lavana's old discarded toys.

1697
02:06:44,646 --> 02:06:45,605
Let's go.

1698
02:07:00,855 --> 02:07:02,812
Here's the last bite. Open up.

1699
02:07:02,813 --> 02:07:04,271
Enough for me, Mom. Feed him.

1700
02:07:17,980 --> 02:07:19,480
<i>Does it hurt? Huh?</i>

1701
02:07:20,021 --> 02:07:21,938
<i>I'm not yelling to save face.</i>

1702
02:07:22,438 --> 02:07:23,605
<i>Imagine how hurt I am.</i>

1703
02:07:25,396 --> 02:07:26,271
Brother?

1704
02:07:27,021 --> 02:07:29,480
Why is Dad hitting Mom like that?

1705
02:07:31,105 --> 02:07:31,980
You really want to know?

1706
02:07:34,313 --> 02:07:36,271
You're not Dad's son, right?

1707
02:07:36,980 --> 02:07:38,730
That's why he's hitting her.

1708
02:07:44,938 --> 02:07:46,188
Hey!

1709
02:07:46,313 --> 02:07:48,229
Get off me!

1710
02:07:48,230 --> 02:07:49,146
What…

1711
02:07:50,521 --> 02:07:51,480
Get off me!

1712
02:07:52,438 --> 02:07:53,355
Leave me!

1713
02:07:54,563 --> 02:07:55,563
Get off me!

1714
02:07:56,646 --> 02:07:58,688
Kusuma, get off me!

1715
02:07:59,521 --> 02:08:00,480
Kusuma!

1716
02:08:09,771 --> 02:08:11,146
Get off!

1717
02:08:11,771 --> 02:08:12,688
Get off!

1718
02:08:19,563 --> 02:08:22,438
- Why did you bite him?
- He said I'm not your son.

1719
02:08:27,688 --> 02:08:29,813
Yes, he's right.

1720
02:08:30,271 --> 02:08:31,313
Who were you born to?

1721
02:08:59,771 --> 02:09:01,230
Happy Birthday, my prince!

1722
02:09:02,021 --> 02:09:03,521
How old did I turn, Mom?

1723
02:09:04,146 --> 02:09:05,104
Eleven.

1724
02:09:05,105 --> 02:09:06,896
How many years to go?

1725
02:09:10,771 --> 02:09:13,104
Mom, I'm hungry.

1726
02:09:13,105 --> 02:09:15,271
Ten minutes, my prince.
Kesari (sweet dish) will be ready.

1727
02:09:20,730 --> 02:09:23,563
Sir! Sir! You'll get a tummy-ache
if you don't remove the seeds.

1728
02:09:23,730 --> 02:09:25,271
I'm hungry.

1729
02:09:25,938 --> 02:09:27,813
Sir, wait, I'll get the seeds out.

1730
02:09:29,146 --> 02:09:32,812
Look, ma'am, he's not listening to me.

1731
02:09:32,813 --> 02:09:34,355
He doesn't listen to
anyone when he's hungry.

1732
02:10:06,230 --> 02:10:07,313
Kusuma, give me the ball.

1733
02:10:09,021 --> 02:10:11,312
Brother? Can I play too?

1734
02:10:11,313 --> 02:10:13,270
Cricket isn't for kids.

1735
02:10:13,271 --> 02:10:14,605
Go play with my old toys.

1736
02:10:31,688 --> 02:10:32,896
Lavanappa, bring him down!

1737
02:10:34,021 --> 02:10:36,105
<i>In a pit,</i>

1738
02:10:36,438 --> 02:10:42,688
<i>a baby crow was cast away.</i>

1739
02:10:43,938 --> 02:10:46,313
<i>Showing no affection,</i>

1740
02:10:46,438 --> 02:10:52,605
<i>the dad grows distant.</i>

1741
02:10:53,938 --> 02:10:58,313
<i>What was the baby crow's</i>

1742
02:10:58,646 --> 02:11:02,938
<i>fault?</i>

1743
02:11:03,980 --> 02:11:08,271
<i>Why such hatred</i>

1744
02:11:08,646 --> 02:11:13,480
<i>in his father?</i>

1745
02:11:26,188 --> 02:11:30,521
<i>Some suspicion</i>

1746
02:11:31,063 --> 02:11:35,730
<i>turned into a raging demon.</i>

1747
02:11:36,355 --> 02:11:38,937
<i>Is it a parasite?</i>

1748
02:11:38,938 --> 02:11:41,105
<i>Did it make us distant?</i>

1749
02:11:41,313 --> 02:11:44,187
<i>Did the father not hear</i>

1750
02:11:44,188 --> 02:11:46,146
<i>his kid weeping?</i>

1751
02:11:46,438 --> 02:11:48,604
<i>Did it leave this nest as
no eye looked its way?</i>

1752
02:11:48,605 --> 02:11:49,562
Dad! Dad!

1753
02:11:49,563 --> 02:11:51,438
Kusuma! Come, Dad!

1754
02:11:51,646 --> 02:11:53,438
- What happened?
- Come, Dad.

1755
02:11:58,438 --> 02:11:59,313
Step aside!

1756
02:11:59,438 --> 02:12:00,438
Move!

1757
02:12:06,063 --> 02:12:07,438
The kid is drowning!

1758
02:12:07,938 --> 02:12:09,396
The kid is drowning!

1759
02:12:09,771 --> 02:12:10,729
Help!

1760
02:12:10,730 --> 02:12:12,230
The kid is drowning!

1761
02:12:12,855 --> 02:12:14,188
Someone please help!

1762
02:12:14,605 --> 02:12:17,230
Hurry up! Come on!

1763
02:12:17,896 --> 02:12:18,813
Hurry!

1764
02:12:40,605 --> 02:12:45,021
<i>What was the baby crow's</i>

1765
02:12:45,271 --> 02:12:49,563
<i>fault?</i>

1766
02:12:50,563 --> 02:12:55,021
<i>Why such hatred</i>

1767
02:12:55,313 --> 02:12:57,812
<i>in his father?</i>

1768
02:12:57,813 --> 02:12:58,771
My prince!

1769
02:13:01,688 --> 02:13:02,688
My prince!

1770
02:13:03,438 --> 02:13:05,062
<i>Some suspicion</i>

1771
02:13:05,063 --> 02:13:07,396
- My prince?
<i>- Some suspicion</i>

1772
02:13:08,188 --> 02:13:12,438
- My prince!
<i>- turned into a raging demon</i>

1773
02:13:13,438 --> 02:13:15,895
<i>Is it a parasite?</i>

1774
02:13:15,896 --> 02:13:18,188
- My prince!
<i>- Did it make us distant?</i>

1775
02:13:18,438 --> 02:13:23,230
<i>Did the father not hear
his kid weeping?</i>

1776
02:13:23,480 --> 02:13:29,646
<i>Did it leave this nest as
no eye looked its way?</i>

1777
02:14:12,688 --> 02:14:14,188
Call sir to pour soil on him.

1778
02:14:14,396 --> 02:14:15,938
I have nothing to do with this.

1779
02:14:17,355 --> 02:14:18,396
It's entirely his fault.

1780
02:14:20,605 --> 02:14:22,146
- His fault.
- Ramudu…

1781
02:14:24,605 --> 02:14:25,605
His fault.

1782
02:14:25,730 --> 02:14:26,688
What's wrong?

1783
02:14:29,021 --> 02:14:30,271
They're calling you to pour soil on him.

1784
02:14:31,521 --> 02:14:32,396
Let's go.

1785
02:14:55,188 --> 02:14:56,271
I have…

1786
02:14:59,271 --> 02:15:01,313
nothing to do with this.

1787
02:15:04,813 --> 02:15:05,855
This is entirely your fault.

1788
02:15:09,313 --> 02:15:10,313
Not mine.

1789
02:15:19,813 --> 02:15:20,730
I didn't…

1790
02:15:23,188 --> 02:15:24,230
It's not my fault.

1791
02:15:26,146 --> 02:15:27,063
It's his fault.

1792
02:15:36,855 --> 02:15:38,855
Ask them to plant it there.

1793
02:15:58,355 --> 02:16:00,230
Unable to bear my father's torture,

1794
02:16:00,730 --> 02:16:04,980
My mother bottled up
her grief over Kusuma's passing.

1795
02:16:05,813 --> 02:16:08,521
Tormented by whether
his doubts were valid,

1796
02:16:09,063 --> 02:16:10,771
my father spiraled into madness.

1797
02:16:16,146 --> 02:16:19,313
Over the years,
I've gotten used to all this.

1798
02:16:19,938 --> 02:16:20,813
Wait!

1799
02:16:22,605 --> 02:16:24,896
But according to the complaint I received,

1800
02:16:25,605 --> 02:16:29,313
Mr. Ramappa bought the kid from
that man's wife for 100 rupees.

1801
02:16:29,730 --> 02:16:33,605
But you say he suspected
Kusuma wasn't his son…

1802
02:16:34,021 --> 02:16:35,938
and tortured your mother.

1803
02:16:39,521 --> 02:16:41,979
The two stories don't match.

1804
02:16:41,980 --> 02:16:43,480
I don't understand it either.

1805
02:16:44,146 --> 02:16:46,437
If the baby was bought,

1806
02:16:46,438 --> 02:16:48,313
why would my father torment my mother?

1807
02:16:48,480 --> 02:16:50,480
Suppose the complaint
you got is fabricated.

1808
02:16:50,646 --> 02:16:52,438
Then my father's doubts remain.

1809
02:16:53,063 --> 02:16:54,230
Look, Inspector,

1810
02:16:54,355 --> 02:16:58,730
these doubts drove my father crazy
and got him bedridden.

1811
02:16:59,188 --> 02:17:00,313
Even if he dies,

1812
02:17:00,688 --> 02:17:02,771
I need to know who's responsible.

1813
02:17:03,438 --> 02:17:06,520
{\an8}Was Kusuma born to
this guy or to my father?

1814
02:17:06,521 --> 02:17:07,605
- Or some other--
- Hey!

1815
02:17:08,396 --> 02:17:11,563
Your father tortured us all this time.
And now, you?

1816
02:17:14,646 --> 02:17:17,438
Inspector, Ramappa is on death bed.

1817
02:17:18,438 --> 02:17:20,896
I don't think he's in a
position to talk to you.

1818
02:17:21,521 --> 02:17:22,521
And another thing,

1819
02:17:22,771 --> 02:17:24,688
Kusuma wasn't bought from anyone.

1820
02:17:25,355 --> 02:17:27,563
He was born in my hospital,
in front of Ramappa's eyes.

1821
02:17:28,355 --> 02:17:29,355
He is his very own child.

1822
02:17:30,480 --> 02:17:32,396
People will tell you a
hundred things, Inspector.

1823
02:17:32,730 --> 02:17:34,313
You don't have to take them seriously.

1824
02:17:36,813 --> 02:17:39,312
- How dare you?
- Keep talking, and I'll tear you apart.

1825
02:17:39,313 --> 02:17:40,354
- What will you do?
- Stay away!

1826
02:17:40,355 --> 02:17:41,355
Sir?

1827
02:17:43,563 --> 02:17:44,438
Come.

1828
02:17:53,271 --> 02:17:54,188
Is it him, sir?

1829
02:17:58,396 --> 02:18:01,105
{\an8}Yes, that's him. Come, sit.

1830
02:18:11,438 --> 02:18:14,271
He is Michael. The man who filed the case.

1831
02:18:14,688 --> 02:18:15,896
Tell us what happened, Michael.

1832
02:18:17,646 --> 02:18:19,605
Inspector, wait a minute.

1833
02:18:21,480 --> 02:18:22,771
- Achchamma?
- Yes?

1834
02:18:23,063 --> 02:18:26,188
- Get back to work.
- It's fine, sir. My work is done.

1835
02:18:26,688 --> 02:18:30,395
Is that so? Then go
attend to Ramudu. Go on.

1836
02:18:30,396 --> 02:18:32,646
- Appa is resting fine.
- Go!

1837
02:18:52,605 --> 02:18:54,813
Lavana sir!

1838
02:19:14,438 --> 02:19:15,438
Achchamma, what happened?

1839
02:19:17,188 --> 02:19:18,105
Where's Dad?

1840
02:19:20,146 --> 02:19:21,355
Ap… Appa…

1841
02:19:29,355 --> 02:19:30,271
Lavana!

1842
02:19:31,230 --> 02:19:32,105
Achari!

1843
02:19:32,980 --> 02:19:33,855
Achchamma!

1844
02:19:35,813 --> 02:19:37,480
Where have you guys
been these past three days?

1845
02:19:39,396 --> 02:19:41,771
Hello! Nice to meet you!

1846
02:19:42,271 --> 02:19:43,730
Bhuvanam Ramappa Rao Bahadur.

1847
02:19:44,646 --> 02:19:46,521
{\an8}- And you?
- I'm Inspector Jagannadhan.

1848
02:19:46,813 --> 02:19:48,104
- Jagannadhan?
- Yes.

1849
02:19:48,105 --> 02:19:48,980
Good.

1850
02:19:51,438 --> 02:19:52,813
And who is he?

1851
02:20:03,980 --> 02:20:05,730
Why are you crying, Mr. Ramappa?

1852
02:20:07,521 --> 02:20:12,354
That poor father's grief
is putting me to tears.

1853
02:20:12,355 --> 02:20:15,605
So, you then agree that Michael
is Kusuma's father?

1854
02:20:17,355 --> 02:20:19,313
What if I say yes?
What if I say no?

1855
02:20:19,563 --> 02:20:20,438
Good question.

1856
02:20:21,230 --> 02:20:23,645
If you agree that Michael
is Kusuma's father,

1857
02:20:23,646 --> 02:20:27,313
since he filed a case that
you killed his son,

1858
02:20:27,563 --> 02:20:29,063
we'll take it to court.

1859
02:20:29,771 --> 02:20:32,438
If it's proven that you killed Kusuma,

1860
02:20:32,563 --> 02:20:38,188
you'd get life imprisonment or
a death sentence. That's it.

1861
02:20:41,438 --> 02:20:43,855
- And if I don't agree?
- If you don't?

1862
02:20:44,521 --> 02:20:46,271
My investigation will continue.

1863
02:20:47,105 --> 02:20:49,229
We'll have the court
authorize an exhumation,

1864
02:20:49,230 --> 02:20:52,895
recover the kid's body, and run DNA tests,

1865
02:20:52,896 --> 02:20:54,313
thus determining the biological father.

1866
02:20:54,521 --> 02:20:57,813
You'll be cleared if you're
proven to be the father.

1867
02:20:58,313 --> 02:21:01,396
But if proven otherwise,

1868
02:21:01,688 --> 02:21:03,229
things will get complicated.

1869
02:21:03,230 --> 02:21:04,313
And, no matter who the father is,

1870
02:21:04,480 --> 02:21:06,521
if we find that you killed the boy,

1871
02:21:07,105 --> 02:21:08,230
you will be jailed.

1872
02:21:10,021 --> 02:21:10,938
Oh?

1873
02:21:12,230 --> 02:21:13,313
Then, I don't agree.

1874
02:21:14,480 --> 02:21:15,355
What do you mean?

1875
02:21:15,896 --> 02:21:18,605
I mean Kusuma is my own son.

1876
02:21:18,896 --> 02:21:20,730
My heir. My blood.

1877
02:21:21,396 --> 02:21:23,980
Why would I agree that
someone else is the father?

1878
02:21:25,105 --> 02:21:27,438
I will cooperate with any investigation.

1879
02:21:29,313 --> 02:21:30,188
Wait a minute.

1880
02:21:40,105 --> 02:21:41,396
So, Mr. Ramappa?

1881
02:21:41,771 --> 02:21:44,146
Will you now agree that
Kusuma is not your son?

1882
02:21:46,105 --> 02:21:47,021
Show me your palm.

1883
02:21:48,855 --> 02:21:50,063
You need samples, right?

1884
02:21:53,355 --> 02:21:54,355
Kusuma's tooth.

1885
02:21:57,896 --> 02:21:58,771
If that's not enough,

1886
02:21:59,355 --> 02:22:00,230
take a look at this.

1887
02:22:01,105 --> 02:22:02,146
Kusuma's little finger.

1888
02:22:05,063 --> 02:22:06,188
If that's not enough either,

1889
02:22:06,688 --> 02:22:07,563
I have more.

1890
02:22:08,396 --> 02:22:09,396
Kusuma's rib.

1891
02:22:13,396 --> 02:22:15,980
Why do you have these?

1892
02:22:17,938 --> 02:22:21,646
We held a ceremony for Kusuma last week.

1893
02:22:22,188 --> 02:22:24,855
I plucked these out as souvenirs.

1894
02:22:27,188 --> 02:22:29,355
Do you not believe me? They're original.

1895
02:22:29,605 --> 02:22:30,563
Here, smell them.

1896
02:22:32,313 --> 02:22:33,271
That way.

1897
02:22:43,021 --> 02:22:44,480
Sorry, I'm a vegetarian.

1898
02:22:45,188 --> 02:22:47,730
When you shoved the finger
into my nose out of nowhere,

1899
02:22:48,230 --> 02:22:49,355
I got nauseous.

1900
02:22:49,730 --> 02:22:55,229
Since we have no evidence
that these are Kusumappa's samples,

1901
02:22:55,230 --> 02:22:58,020
we will follow protocol and
come with our forensic team,

1902
02:22:58,021 --> 02:23:01,938
dig up the grave, and take samples.

1903
02:23:02,188 --> 02:23:04,230
Oh, no! Why dig it up, Inspector?

1904
02:23:04,480 --> 02:23:07,813
I've prepared a path.
Let me show you.

1905
02:23:07,938 --> 02:23:08,896
Move aside!

1906
02:23:11,188 --> 02:23:14,688
{\an8}Look! There's that tree, and
right under it is the grave.

1907
02:23:15,063 --> 02:23:17,105
{\an8}See that door beside it, on the ground.

1908
02:23:17,688 --> 02:23:20,521
That door will lead
you straight to Kusuma.

1909
02:23:21,230 --> 02:23:23,688
I felt there would be a need for--

1910
02:23:25,355 --> 02:23:26,271
Oh…

1911
02:23:31,271 --> 02:23:32,271
I mean,

1912
02:23:32,688 --> 02:23:36,729
I designed it to visit him

1913
02:23:36,730 --> 02:23:38,396
whenever I missed him.

1914
02:23:48,355 --> 02:23:49,438
<i>You see, Mr. Lavana,</i>

1915
02:23:50,146 --> 02:23:52,521
as your father is mentally unstable,

1916
02:23:52,771 --> 02:23:56,063
it's difficult to say whether
he's lying or not.

1917
02:23:56,521 --> 02:23:59,063
So, this case seems to be getting bigger.

1918
02:23:59,396 --> 02:24:00,730
What did my father even tell you?

1919
02:24:02,771 --> 02:24:03,813
{\an8}Do you really want to know?

1920
02:24:05,855 --> 02:24:08,605
{\an8}He claimed that Kusuma is his own son…

1921
02:24:09,438 --> 02:24:11,980
{\an8}and said they share the same blood.

1922
02:24:21,688 --> 02:24:22,938
By the way, Dr. Achari,

1923
02:24:23,563 --> 02:24:26,313
when I asked your friend why
he keeps falling unconscious,

1924
02:24:26,813 --> 02:24:27,688
He said, "That's just how I am".

1925
02:24:27,813 --> 02:24:32,146
"Sometimes, I enter into a
meditative state. Like Jesus."

1926
02:24:32,688 --> 02:24:35,938
Make sure nothing like this
happens until the case is closed.

1927
02:24:36,355 --> 02:24:38,896
It won't happen, Inspector.

1928
02:24:39,730 --> 02:24:43,230
He won't sleep or let others
sleep until this case is closed.

1929
02:24:51,688 --> 02:24:52,646
Sorry, uncle.

1930
02:24:53,480 --> 02:24:56,313
I got furious
and insulted you for no reason.

1931
02:24:59,188 --> 02:25:00,313
It's alright, Lavana.

1932
02:25:04,021 --> 02:25:06,480
If the case proves that
Kusuma was born to my father,

1933
02:25:06,855 --> 02:25:07,730
it's fine.

1934
02:25:08,396 --> 02:25:11,063
It's also fine if it's proved that
he was born to that man.

1935
02:25:13,396 --> 02:25:16,271
But if neither of them
turns out to be his father…

1936
02:25:22,021 --> 02:25:23,980
Let's go check on my father.

1937
02:25:50,813 --> 02:25:53,063
Hasn't the grave been dug yet?

1938
02:25:53,730 --> 02:25:55,813
Not there. It's here.

1939
02:25:59,313 --> 02:26:00,438
See this door?

1940
02:26:00,896 --> 02:26:04,396
It leads straight to the kid's body.

1941
02:26:04,980 --> 02:26:08,355
How strange!
Never seen anything like it.

1942
02:26:08,855 --> 02:26:10,771
- Right, Senior?
- Yes, Junior.

1943
02:26:10,896 --> 02:26:11,771
I haven't either.

1944
02:26:12,355 --> 02:26:16,105
This is nothing. There are far
stranger things inside the house.

1945
02:26:16,396 --> 02:26:17,771
This is just a pinch of salt.

1946
02:26:49,396 --> 02:26:51,980
Did you get all the samples you need?

1947
02:26:52,480 --> 02:26:56,105
Yes. But they seem to have
over-watered this tree.

1948
02:26:56,646 --> 02:27:00,854
{\an8}- Testing might be a bit tricky.
- No. Please don't say that.

1949
02:27:00,855 --> 02:27:03,480
{\an8}- All hell will break loose.
- Don't worry, Inspector.

1950
02:27:03,688 --> 02:27:05,896
We said it was tricky, not impossible.

1951
02:27:07,105 --> 02:27:10,105
Since they didn't use
salt water, it's alright.

1952
02:27:10,646 --> 02:27:11,605
Right, Senior?

1953
02:27:12,063 --> 02:27:15,438
I was going to say that.
But he panicked before I could, Junior.

1954
02:27:15,896 --> 02:27:18,646
{\an8}So, when can we expect the reports?

1955
02:27:19,980 --> 02:27:21,313
- Two weeks?
- Two weeks.

1956
02:27:21,688 --> 02:27:23,105
- That's it. Two weeks.
- That's it. Two weeks.

1957
02:27:23,521 --> 02:27:25,605
We'll submit the reports in court.

1958
02:27:25,980 --> 02:27:27,480
Good. Let's go.

1959
02:27:46,105 --> 02:27:47,396
Two more weeks.

1960
02:27:54,105 --> 02:27:55,021
Appa?

1961
02:27:55,730 --> 02:27:57,146
Get up, I brought food.

1962
02:28:09,396 --> 02:28:10,271
Appa?

1963
02:28:13,396 --> 02:28:14,271
Appa?

1964
02:28:24,521 --> 02:28:25,730
Lavana sir!

1965
02:28:30,188 --> 02:28:31,271
Lavana sir!

1966
02:28:36,813 --> 02:28:37,688
Appa!

1967
02:28:40,355 --> 02:28:41,438
He's stuck like this.

1968
02:28:43,521 --> 02:28:45,855
Hey, I'm telling you the truth.

1969
02:28:47,063 --> 02:28:48,688
See for yourself, come.

1970
02:28:51,605 --> 02:28:52,730
Hello, Mr. Chidambaram?

1971
02:28:53,855 --> 02:28:55,230
Look, Dr. Achari.

1972
02:28:56,021 --> 02:28:59,313
When you said he got up and
started drinking again,

1973
02:28:59,730 --> 02:29:02,355
I considered quitting my practice.

1974
02:29:02,855 --> 02:29:06,188
But continued due to
pressure from my family.

1975
02:29:06,896 --> 02:29:11,021
I don't think I have enough
medical knowledge to diagnose him.

1976
02:29:11,438 --> 02:29:15,271
So, it is better to see
some senior doctor.

1977
02:29:17,271 --> 02:29:21,980
See, we still have to diagnose
his mental disorder.

1978
02:29:23,063 --> 02:29:27,063
This is a rare symptom of
some psychological disorders.

1979
02:29:27,688 --> 02:29:31,980
The victim remains motionless for hours.

1980
02:29:32,646 --> 02:29:35,646
But five days? It's weird.

1981
02:29:39,480 --> 02:29:41,730
It's better we give him some fluid foods

1982
02:29:41,938 --> 02:29:43,063
till he becomes normal.

1983
02:29:47,230 --> 02:29:50,480
<i>Only two more weeks.</i>

1984
02:29:50,688 --> 02:29:54,021
<i>Only two more weeks.</i>

1985
02:29:57,980 --> 02:29:59,313
<i>Two weeks.</i>

1986
02:29:59,730 --> 02:30:01,063
<i>Two weeks.</i>

1987
02:30:12,105 --> 02:30:13,438
The judge has arrived.

1988
02:30:14,021 --> 02:30:15,770
Check if Michael is inside.

1989
02:30:15,771 --> 02:30:16,813
- Okay.
- Yes.

1990
02:30:48,896 --> 02:30:50,105
Mr. Ramappa!

1991
02:30:51,146 --> 02:30:52,230
You seem to be glowing!

1992
02:30:54,396 --> 02:30:56,563
I just came out of my meditative sleep.

1993
02:30:57,480 --> 02:31:00,063
That's the reason behind this glow.

1994
02:31:00,271 --> 02:31:03,438
Please share the secret.
We'll follow it too.

1995
02:31:05,021 --> 02:31:06,563
It can't be taught.

1996
02:31:06,896 --> 02:31:07,771
Then?

1997
02:31:08,271 --> 02:31:11,730
It's a superpower you gain
when life goes to shits.

1998
02:31:12,813 --> 02:31:13,688
That's so funny.

1999
02:31:14,980 --> 02:31:15,855
No.

2000
02:31:17,230 --> 02:31:19,230
- I'm serious.
- Ramudu!

2001
02:31:25,355 --> 02:31:27,021
I was so worried about you.

2002
02:31:28,855 --> 02:31:29,896
Is the job done?

2003
02:31:31,105 --> 02:31:31,980
All set.

2004
02:31:33,730 --> 02:31:34,605
Let's go.

2005
02:31:35,396 --> 02:31:36,438
Let's find the truth.

2006
02:31:38,188 --> 02:31:39,105
Ramudu!

2007
02:31:40,521 --> 02:31:42,980
You can't enter the court with a turban.

2008
02:32:34,021 --> 02:32:35,813
It must be something sketchy

2009
02:32:35,938 --> 02:32:37,521
if I was asked to come here in the dark.

2010
02:32:38,480 --> 02:32:41,813
The result may or may not prove
Kusuma as Ramappa's son.

2011
02:32:42,271 --> 02:32:43,688
But it definitely won't
say Michael is the dad.

2012
02:32:44,146 --> 02:32:45,021
How are you so sure?

2013
02:32:46,771 --> 02:32:49,313
Because I was the one
who sent Michael to you.

2014
02:32:49,563 --> 02:32:51,230
- What?
- Yes.

2015
02:32:56,021 --> 02:32:59,271
This test is the only
way to clear my name.

2016
02:33:00,271 --> 02:33:02,521
And for that, I need a police case.

2017
02:33:03,980 --> 02:33:07,396
- So, I sent Michael-
- You sent Michael to file a fake case.

2018
02:33:07,646 --> 02:33:08,563
I got it.

2019
02:33:09,563 --> 02:33:10,480
Trust me, I got it.

2020
02:33:17,063 --> 02:33:20,313
This is for you to spare Michael.

2021
02:33:21,271 --> 02:33:25,521
Having considered the evidence
and arguments of both parties,

2022
02:33:25,813 --> 02:33:31,605
the court finds no conspiracy behind
Kusumappa Raju's death

2023
02:33:32,063 --> 02:33:35,146
and declares it a suicide.

2024
02:33:37,021 --> 02:33:39,646
The court will now disclose
the DNA test results.

2025
02:33:39,980 --> 02:33:43,021
Firstly, the probability of paternity…

2026
02:33:43,480 --> 02:33:48,605
in the DNA report of
Mr. Michael Sahayam is 0%.

2027
02:33:50,188 --> 02:33:53,354
Next, the probability of paternity…

2028
02:33:53,355 --> 02:33:57,980
in the DNA report of
Mr. Bhuvanam Ramappa Rao Bahadur

2029
02:33:58,230 --> 02:34:00,730
is 99.9%.

2030
02:34:01,021 --> 02:34:04,938
Hence, the court declares Mr. Rao
Bahadur as the biological father of…

2031
02:34:05,313 --> 02:34:10,313
deceased child Kusumappa Raju,
as established by the DNA results.

2032
02:34:18,730 --> 02:34:19,605
Lawyer!

2033
02:34:19,938 --> 02:34:21,021
Yes, Mr. Ramappa?

2034
02:34:22,730 --> 02:34:24,480
I have my doubts about this judge.

2035
02:34:25,980 --> 02:34:27,938
I won't believe it unless
I see the report myself.

2036
02:34:29,105 --> 02:34:30,105
Alright.

2037
02:34:58,105 --> 02:35:01,646
Mr. Ramappa, the judge
wants the document back.

2038
02:35:21,896 --> 02:35:23,563
Please fulfill my last wish and

2039
02:35:23,855 --> 02:35:27,438
free me from the curse of this jar.

2040
02:35:46,146 --> 02:35:49,355
Ma'am, Appa is no more.

2041
02:35:49,688 --> 02:35:50,855
Ma'am!

2042
02:36:31,605 --> 02:36:35,563
Relatives and friends, may go one by one,

2043
02:36:35,688 --> 02:36:41,020
say three times his name in his ear,

2044
02:36:41,021 --> 02:36:44,355
and tell him anything one wants,
for the last time.

2045
02:37:21,396 --> 02:37:22,271
Dear,

2046
02:37:25,271 --> 02:37:26,771
please forgive me.

2047
02:37:27,605 --> 02:37:29,521
I've kept a secret from you.

2048
02:37:36,980 --> 02:37:37,938
La…

2049
02:37:39,688 --> 02:37:40,563
Lavana…

2050
02:37:41,771 --> 02:37:43,271
is not your son.

2051
02:38:06,313 --> 02:38:07,188
Ramudu,

2052
02:38:08,521 --> 02:38:10,230
I may have kept a lot of secrets from you.

2053
02:38:11,646 --> 02:38:13,521
But I genuinely wanted
to tell you this for so long.

2054
02:38:14,146 --> 02:38:15,021
I just couldn't.

2055
02:38:16,355 --> 02:38:17,355
Forgive me.

2056
02:38:19,438 --> 02:38:20,355
You…

2057
02:38:22,188 --> 02:38:23,521
you are not your father's son.

2058
02:38:54,896 --> 02:38:56,396
I have some good news for you.

2059
02:39:11,563 --> 02:39:13,188
That's great. Who's the father?

2060
02:39:38,230 --> 02:39:39,146
Renuka!

2061
02:39:45,021 --> 02:39:46,105
Don't say no, Renuka.

2062
02:39:46,771 --> 02:39:48,730
He's hell-bent on marrying you.

2063
02:39:52,188 --> 02:39:54,730
His father's death has
disturbed him mentally.

2064
02:39:55,146 --> 02:39:58,105
This marriage might
help him recover from it.

2065
02:40:00,605 --> 02:40:01,938
There's a truth you must know.

2066
02:40:02,813 --> 02:40:04,187
Forget it.

2067
02:40:04,188 --> 02:40:06,688
We all have our own set of truths.

2068
02:40:07,521 --> 02:40:09,104
One's truth is nobody else's business.

2069
02:40:09,105 --> 02:40:11,230
I won't ask you anything.
You don't tell me either.

2070
02:40:13,521 --> 02:40:14,980
But the truth is--

2071
02:40:15,605 --> 02:40:16,771
There we go again!

2072
02:40:17,230 --> 02:40:18,730
You don't have to reveal any truths.

2073
02:40:23,063 --> 02:40:25,771
Okay. I'll think about
it and let you know.

2074
02:40:37,146 --> 02:40:38,438
Give it a good thought.

2075
02:40:38,855 --> 02:40:40,771
He's definitely not the
gentleman you knew before.

2076
02:41:25,521 --> 02:41:27,730
<i>I lost both my wife and child
at childbirth.</i>

2077
02:41:27,896 --> 02:41:30,646
<i>Now they torment me with questions about</i>

2078
02:41:30,980 --> 02:41:32,188
<i>who will carry the lineage forward!</i>

2079
02:41:32,938 --> 02:41:35,105
Why don't you marry again?

2080
02:41:37,396 --> 02:41:40,605
There's no room in my heart
for anyone but Vasudha.

2081
02:41:41,813 --> 02:41:43,313
So, what are you planning to do?

2082
02:41:43,938 --> 02:41:45,896
I'm thinking of adopting a kid.

2083
02:41:46,855 --> 02:41:48,521
Sadly, she died at childbirth.

2084
02:41:49,271 --> 02:41:50,771
I'll announce that
only the child survived…

2085
02:41:51,563 --> 02:41:53,730
and introduce him
to the world as my heir.

2086
02:42:03,396 --> 02:42:05,355
- How much did it cost?
- Hundred rupees.

2087
02:42:06,105 --> 02:42:08,605
Here. Don't ask where I got him from.

2088
02:42:09,105 --> 02:42:11,063
He is my gift to the Bhuvana Dynasty.

2089
02:42:26,688 --> 02:42:28,771
BHUVANA'S ESTATE

2090
02:42:37,938 --> 02:42:39,188
I'm telling you, move away!

2091
02:42:41,146 --> 02:42:42,271
Get out of my way!

2092
02:42:43,271 --> 02:42:44,896
Is this today's item?

2093
02:42:46,230 --> 02:42:47,230
Let's chuck it out.

2094
02:42:47,855 --> 02:42:48,730
Oh!

2095
02:42:49,146 --> 02:42:50,521
Sandalwood!

2096
02:42:50,980 --> 02:42:52,230
It's an expensive death.

2097
02:42:55,938 --> 02:42:57,938
Big man has died with his eyes open.

2098
02:43:03,105 --> 02:43:03,980
Hey!

2099
02:43:04,688 --> 02:43:06,313
Is this arrogance
because you're sandalwood?

2100
02:43:13,105 --> 02:43:14,063
Again?!

2101
02:43:16,896 --> 02:43:18,730
The arrogance isn't coming
from this piece of wood.

2102
02:43:19,230 --> 02:43:20,521
It's coming from this piece of wood.

2103
02:43:21,105 --> 02:43:22,563
I'll set it right.

2104
02:43:27,563 --> 02:43:29,063
Careful! He's a royal.

2105
02:43:30,980 --> 02:43:32,313
Royal, huh?

2106
02:43:33,855 --> 02:43:36,480
Come back in a bit to collect
the ashes and gold.

